// 자동 생성 파일: tools/parse_exam.py
window.EXAM_DATA = {"2022":{"sections":["Choose the one that is closest in meaning to the underlined word(s).","Choose the one that best fills in the blank.","Choose the one that most grammatically completes the sentence.","Choose the one that is grammatically INCORRECT.","Choose the one(s) that best complete(s) the sentence.","Read the following passages and answer the questions."],"passages":["More than two decades after the last train traveled down the line, the High Line is now one of the most innovative and inviting public spaces in all of New York City. From the day it opened in June 2009, it has been one of the city’s major tourist attractions. It is unlike any other experience in the city. The black steel columns allow you to float 25 feet above the ground; without streets to cross or traffic lights to wait for, you can walk ten blocks as quickly as two down below. You can sit surrounded by nature and take in the sun and the Hudson River views, or you can walk the line between old buildings and past striking new ones.","There was this person at the University of Virginia Hospital. Kept getting admitted for weird stomach complaints. (A) The doctors were twisting themselves inside out to figure it out. (B) He’d get better; his wife would come in to see him in the hospital and bring him banana pudding. (C) Someone finally ordered a toxicity test on him, but he was discharged before the results came back: off the charts for arsenic. (D) We called the wife Banana Pudding Lily.","All the places for new students had been taken at a prestigious elementary school in London, England. The school had a waiting list. Any places that opened up would be offered to children at the top of the list. One child (let’s call her Wendy) was near, but not at, the top. Adjacent to her on the list, one step higher, was another girl (let’s call her Jane). Wendy’s mother set up an email account in the name of Jane’s mother and sent the school an email asking them to remove Jane from the waiting list. Consequently, Wendy rose one step.","Business before the financial crisis in 1997 in Korea was more like a club. But the crisis broke apart the cozy government-banking-corporate networks, forcing the big companies to become truly profitable, independent and internationally competitive for the first time. Now there’s a lot more competition, and that’s for the first time. Now there’s a lot more competition, and that’s forcing companies to be innovative.","No one knows for sure what caused Edison’s hearing problems, but after the age of twelve he could no longer hear birds singing. As a teenager working in a telegraph office jammed with clattering telegraph machines, he viewed his poor hearing as a distinct advantage because he could focus on his instrument on his desk and not be distracted. As a renowned inventor, he received pleas from hearing-impaired people all over the world to invent a hearing aid, but he declined, believing this so-called disability gave him valuable mental space in which to think.","The digital world offers us many advantages, but if we yield to that world too completely we may lose the privacy we need to develop a self. Activities that require time and careful attention, like serious reading, are at risk; we read less and skim more as the Internet occupies more of our lives. And there’s a link between self-hood and reading slowly, rather than scanning for quick information, as the Web encourages us to do. Recent work in sociology and psychology suggests that reading books, a private experience, is an important aspect of coming to know who we are.","Salt has been used as a preservative for thousands of years, and, thanks to some basic and other quite complicated substances, we have \"fresh\" vegetables in January, peanut butter that doesn’t stick to the roof of the mouth, stackable potato chips, and meat that doesn’t turn green on the way home from the grocery store. But as they say, there’s a price to pay for everything. In the case of vegetables and fruits, the price is taste.","Scientists believe they have collected conclusive evidence, or proof, that Ludwig van Beethoven died of lead poisoning. They used the most powerful X-ray beam in the Western Hemisphere on six of the famous composer’s hairs and a few pieces of his skull. The results excite scientists because they confirm earlier hints, or clues, that lead caused Beethoven’s death. Beethoven had poor health for many years, and his death, in 1827 at age 56, was long and painful.","The human body has a “set point,” a preferred weight at which it likes to stay. The set point naturally controls body weight to stay within a range of 10 to 20 percent. In most adults, their metabolism allows the energy they make by eating food to be balanced by the amount of energy they use to work and move. _______________________________. This helps their weight to remain stable over a long period of time. However, when people suddenly and significantly decrease or increase their amount of food, their bodies work against the change and try to stay at the set point. Even worse, if a diet causes a rapid loss of a large amount of weight, certain chemicals in the body will quickly increase and make the dieter hungrier. This is the body fighting back to defend its comfortable set point.","A long life is not just the result of being good to your body and _____________ disease. All the various factors that constitute and influence daily life can be critical too. In searching for the ingredients to a long, healthy existence, scientists are studying links between longevity and the psychological and social aspects of human existence. The following can play significant roles in determining your longevity: social integration, autonomy, stress and job satisfaction, etc.","(A) The pandemic has made it hard to visit museums and galleries. But sometimes, we can find art outside in the neighborhood. Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, is known for its murals. Mural Arts Philadelphia has helped create nearly 4,000 of them. Often, these works represent the neighborhood in which they appear. Lisa Murch, director of art education at Mural Arts Philadelphia, says; “Art really belongs to everybody and should be everywhere.” (B) COVID-19 has temporarily changed mural making. Artists have to practice social distancing. They are unable to work on the murals together in person. Murch says some artists are painting pieces of murals at home. The pieces will later be put on a wall. They’ll fit together like a giant puzzle. Murch feels the youth program is crucial during the pandemic. “Art is a really freeing way of expressing a lot of things,” she says. “During this time of stress and anxiety, I think that’s a wonderful thing for kids to access.” (C) Mural Arts runs a youth program. The group teaches kids how to make murals. Students get a chance to work with professional artists. Alaina Ewins joined Mural Arts when she was 13. She’s now a teaching artist for the program. Ewins’s first big project was a mural inside her local youth center. “We got to design the mural and paint it, which was awesome,” she says. Ewins likes to see how making murals affects a neighborhood. Collaboration with people in the community is important, she feels. Artists work with people in the neighborhood to design murals."],"questions":[{"q":1,"stem":"Printed textbooks are rapidly being replaced by ebooks, which harness the interactive capabilities of handheld devices and take pupils beyond the static page with a simple swipe and tap of the finger.","opts":["exploit","restrict","contract","welcome"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":0,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"‘harness’는 ‘(말 따위에) 견인줄을 채우다’ 혹은 ‘동력화하다, 이용하다’라는 의미이다. 따라서 보기에 나온 단어들 중에서는 ‘~의 특색을 살리다, 이용하다’를 뜻하는 ‘exploit’가 가장 의미가 유사하다. ‘contract (계약하다, 질병에 걸리다)’, ‘restrict (제 한하다)’, ‘welcome (환영하다)’ 등은 답으로 적합하지 않다."},{"q":2,"stem":"It is so easy to become apathetic about the environment when we are busy with day-to-day life.","opts":["lame","futile","shrewd","indifferent"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":0,"psg":null,"a":4,"ex":"‘apathetic’은 ‘냉담한, 무관심한’ 이라는 의미를 가지고 있으므로 의미가 유사한 단 어는 ‘indifferent (무관심한)’이다. ‘lame (절름발이의, 불완전한)’, ‘futile (무익한, 하찮은)’, ‘shrewd (예민한, 날카로운)’ 등은 답으로 적합하지 않다."},{"q":3,"stem":"Large groups of carnivores follow more than two million large herbivores during the Great Migrations in Serengeti.","opts":["preys","reptiles","predators","amphibians"],"pts":2.0,"inline":false,"sec":0,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"‘carnivore(육식동물)’들이 ‘herbivore(초식동물)’들을 따라다닌다는 의미이므로 가장 적절한 동의어는 ‘predator(포식자)’이다. ‘prey’(먹이), ‘reptile(파충류)’, ‘amphibian (양서류)’ 등은 답으로 적합하지 않다."},{"q":4,"stem":"Some criminal experts contend that teenagers growing up in depraved areas are far more likely to turn to crime and drug abuse.","opts":["corrupt","secluded","dejected","unpopulated"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":0,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"‘deprave’는 ‘타락시키다, 부패시키다’의 의미이다. 따라서 과거분사형의 ‘depraved’ 와 의미가 가장 유사한 단어는 ‘부패한, 타락한’이라는 뜻의 ‘corrupt’이다."},{"q":5,"stem":"A day or two later, when she was making no progress and was suffering terribly, we began to back off treatment. When she complained of pain, we gave her plenty of morphine. A great plenty. Soon she died quietly and not in pain.","opts":["resist","furnish","abandon","reimburse"],"pts":3.0,"inline":false,"sec":0,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"‘back off’는 ‘그만두다, 물러나다, 철회하다’라는 의미로, 보기의 단어들 중에 ‘abandon’이 의미가 가장 유사하다. ‘furnish (필요한 물건을 제공하다)’, ‘reimburse (배상하다)’, ‘resist (저항하다)’ 등은 답으로 적합하지 않다."},{"q":6,"stem":"Different _________ of G, T, C and A carry different genetic information.","opts":["remains","sequences","conjugations","reinforcements"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":1,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"각각 다른 유전자 정보를 전달하는 ‘염기서열’에 대한 표현으로 ‘sequence (연속, 연쇄)’를 찾을 수 있는지 확인하는 문제이다."},{"q":7,"stem":"Evan was unable to take the chemistry course because the professor _____________ the class at 25 students.","opts":["capped","conned","collected","confined"],"pts":3.0,"inline":false,"sec":1,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"교수가 한 반의 인원을 25명으로 제한했다는 내용이므로, 빈 칸에는 ‘cap’ 이 들어 가야 한다. ‘인원이 ~로 제한되다’라고 할 때 ‘be capped at’ 라는 표현을 쓴다. ‘con’은 ‘정독하다, 배우다, 자세히 조사하다’, ‘collect’는 ‘모으다, 수집하다’, ‘confine’은 ‘어떤 공간에 가두다’라는 뜻이므로 부적합하다."},{"q":8,"stem":"However vague and ____________ the reason for his strange behavior may be, we must try to understand it.","opts":["intimate","imminent","intangible","intensive"],"pts":2.0,"inline":false,"sec":1,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"앞의 내용과 뒤의 내용이 서로 상반되는 문장구조로 되어 있다. 또한 빈칸에는 앞에 오는 ‘모호한, 애매한’이란 의미의 vague와 연결될 수 있는 형용사가 필요하다. 따라서 ‘파악하기 힘든, 이해하기 힘든’이라는 의미의 ‘intangible’이 가장 적합하다."},{"q":9,"stem":"Full-time lecturers who want to be reimbursed for travel costs must __________________________.","opts":["verify their receipts to keep expenses","verify their expenses to keep receipts","keep expenses verifying their receipts","keep receipts verifying their expenses"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":4,"ex":"출장비에 관해 환급을 받으려면 ‘경비를 증명하는 영수증을 보관해야 한다’는 의미가 되어야 하므로 ④가 정답이다."},{"q":10,"stem":"Data compiled by government agencies suggest that ___________ breakfast to school-age children has lessened behavior problems.","opts":["provide","providing","provided","being provided"],"pts":2.0,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"that 절 안에서 동명사 주어를 찾는 문제이므로 ‘providing’이 정답이다. ‘학령 아동 들에게 아침을 제공하는 것이 행동상의 문제들을 줄어들게 했다’는 내용이다."},{"q":11,"stem":"Imagine your grandmother looking like a teenager, playing soccer, and partying at the clubs all night. Or imagine your grandfather teaching you the latest high-tech computer software while listening to loud heavy-metal music. Such a scenario is hard to envision because we ________________ aging and the resulting suffering and death as an unavoidable fact of life.","opts":["are taught to accept","are learned to accept","are learning to be accepted","are teaching to be accepted"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"‘그러한 시나리오는 상상하기 어렵다, 왜냐하면 우리는 노령과 그 결과의 고통 및 죽음을 불가피한 인생의 사실로 받아들이도록 배우기 때문’ 이라는 내용이다. 우리가 ‘배운다’는 것은 ‘we learn’ 혹은 ‘we are taught’로 표현해야 하고, ‘받아들이다’라는 부분은 ‘to accept’ 라는 능동 표현이 되어야 하므로 답은 ①번의 ‘are taught to accept’ 이다."},{"q":12,"stem":"The party’s members were thrilled to win so many seats in the parliament, but ___________ the news that they had overturned the majority.","opts":["still was better","better still was","it was still better","still better it was"],"pts":3.0,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"but 이하의 문장(‘that 이하의 소식이 훨씬 더 좋다’)은 도치되어 있다. the news가 주어이고 was가 동사이며 보어는 good의 비교급인 better이다. still은 비교급을 수식하는 부사로 비교급 앞이나 뒤에 올 수 있다. 주어가 동사 뒤에 가 있으므로 동사와 보어의 자리가 도치되어야 한다."},{"q":13,"stem":"Prior to the product launch, managers had to provide additional training to ___________ of their sales force.","opts":["many","a few","much","several"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"force의 의미와 문법적인 측면(집합적으로 ‘성원(成員), 부원’)을 알고 있는지 확인하는 문제이다. sales force는 ‘판매부서원’을 의미하면서 집합명사로 단수로 취급되므로 ③ much만 답이 될 수 있다."},{"q":14,"stem":"Anyone _____________ for a train to arrive should check the posted schedule for delays and cancellations.","opts":["waiting","who wait","who waiting","whoever is waiting"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"‘Anyone (who is) waiting for~(기다리는 사람은 누구든지)’의 문법적인 표현을 찾는 문제이다. ‘관계대명사 주격 + be동사 (who is)’는 함께 생략될 수 있지만 ③ who waiting처럼 be동사만 생략되거나 ④ whoever(=anyone who)와 같은 표현은 문 법적이지 않다."},{"q":15,"stem":"Animals mate to produce offspring ①that their genes are passed along. Due to their need to reproduce, it seems like ②finding a mating partner should be a straightforward process. Actually, many animals have to ③resort to tactics or tricks to find a partner. Some animals stand out because they look unique, while ④others perform dramatic rituals to woo a mate.","opts":["that their","finding a","resort to","others perform"],"pts":2.5,"inline":true,"sec":3,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"동물들은 유전자가 전해질 수 있도록 자손을 만들기 위해 짝짓기를 한다는 의미가 되어야 하므로 ①의 ‘that’은 목적을 나타내는 접속사 ‘so that’이 되어야 한다. 혹은 along 다음에 전치사가 와서 that이 전치사의 목적격 관계대명사가 되어도 가능하다. ②의 ‘finding’은 it seems like (that) 이후의 절 안에서 주어로 기능한다. ③의 ‘resort to + 명사’는 ~에 의존하다는 의미로 자연스럽다. ④의 ‘others’는 앞의 전체 중의 일부를 나타내는 ‘some’과 짝을 지어 다른 일부를 나타낼 때 쓰는 표현이므로 적절하다."},{"q":16,"stem":"It was an eye-opening experience. Delegations of young people ①had come to Cuba from all over the world. I learned ②how impoverished some other kids were and about the struggles they were going through. When I went home I felt I had a responsibility to do something, to use the information I ③have gained and ④become more active.","opts":["had come","how impoverished","have gained","become more"],"pts":3.0,"inline":true,"sec":3,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"쿠바에서 있었던 세계적 집회에서의 경험을 소개하면서 ‘내가 집에 왔을 때 뭔가를해야 한다는 의무감을 느꼈고, 내가 얻었던 정보를 이용하고 좀 더 적극적인 행동을 해야겠다고 느꼈다’는 내용이다. 내가 ‘느꼈던’ 것이 이미 과거 시제이므로, 그보다 더 이전에 얻은 쿠바에서의 정보는 과거완료 시제가 되어야 한다. 그러므로 ③번이 정답이며 ‘had gained’가 되어야 한다."},{"q":17,"stem":"A marketing plan, administered by a marketing director, includes what to name the product, how to advertise it, how to price it, how to package it, and how to convince customers to buy it. In short, the goal of marketing is to ___________ a shopper's choices toward a single, specific product.","opts":["create","attempt","channel","dominate"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"‘channel’이 명사로 ‘운하’를 뜻하지만 동사로 ‘(관심, 노력 등을) 일정 방향으로 쏠 리게 하다’라는 뜻이 있다. 마케팅의 목표가 ‘구매자의 선택을 구체적인 하나의 제품으로 쏠리게 하는 것’ 이라는 뜻이므로 ③번이 정답이다."},{"q":18,"stem":"The simple, ideal diet―often called the “peasant diet”―is the traditional cuisine of the relatively poor, ___________ countries. It’s usually based on grain (rice, wheat, corn), fruits and vegetables, small amounts of meat, eggs or dairy products, and legumes.","opts":["agrarian","populous","commercial","industrialized"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"빈 칸에는 뒤에 오는 countries를 수식하면서 앞에 오는 ‘peasants (농부)’와도 자연 스럽게 연결되는 형용사가 들어가야 한다. 따라서 ‘농업의’를 뜻하는 ‘agrarian’이 적 절하다. 뒤에서 식이요법에 포함되는 음식들도 대부분 농사를 통해 얻을 수 있는 것 들이다."},{"q":19,"stem":"So many cities face the same challenge of aging infrastructure. And rooftop farming is a terrific way of making use of these industrial buildings. And then of course, they really have such a tremendous environmental benefit to the ecosystem. At the small scale at which it’s practiced in cities around the world, it’s a drop in the bucket, but _________________, we can really create a tidal shift.","opts":["if we can gain some momentum","if this is a minimal beautification project","if it is a great opportunity just to dive into","if we don’t realize our passion until we are out there"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"노후화되는 기간시설물(aging infrastructure)에 옥상정원을 만듦으로써 환경 친화적 인 에코시스템에 기여할 수 있다는 내용이다. 그것이 양동이에 물 한 방울일지라도 ① ‘gain momentum (탄력이 생기다)’ 하게 되면 ‘tidal shift (거대한 변혁)’을 이루어 낼 수 있다는 의미이다."},{"q":20,"stem":"Each year, the National Association of Colleges and Employers asks employers which abilities they want college graduates to possess. At or near the top of that list each year is “analytical reasoning,” a kind of critical thinking skill. Yet accounting majors might ask, “Aren’t mathematical and business skills more important for a career as an accountant?” (A) , nursing majors might suggest that knowledge of medicine is more important for them. Although accountants and nurses obviously need these skills, they must also have a full complement of higher-order thinking skills. People in these kinds of careers must be prepared to solve difficult problems by applying their knowledge to new situations. (B) , they must be able to decide which new ideas they should accept or reject and be able to justify their decisions. On any given day, people in these careers, and most of the careers you may be considering after college, must be able to effectively use critical thinking skills.","opts":["(A) Similarly (B) Moreover","(A) However (B) Moreover","(A) However (B) Therefore","(A) Similarly (B) For instance"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":4,"ex":"연결어를 묻는 문제이다. (A)의 앞에는 회계 전공자가 회계에 필요한 지식이 분석적 사고(analytical reasoning)보다 더 중요한 것이 아닌지 반문한다. (A)의 뒤에는 간호 학 전공자가 의학 지식이 더 중요한 것이 아닌지 반문하므로 ‘유사하게’를 뜻하는 ‘Similarly’가 적절하다. (B)의 앞에는 새로운 상황에 맞닥뜨렸을 때 각자가 가진 지식을 활용하여 어려운 문제를 풀 수 있어야 한다는 내용이 나오고, 뒤에는 어려운 문제 라 할 만한 상황들이 예로 제시된다. 따라서 ‘예를 들어’라는 ‘For instance’가 적절하다."},{"q":21,"stem":"I watched Vincent and Winston play during Christmas week. The chess board seemed to hold elaborate secrets __________________________. The chessmen were more powerful than old Li's magic herbs that cured ancestral curses. And my brothers wore such serious faces that I was sure something was at stake that was greater than avoiding the tradesmen's door to Hong Sing's.","opts":["waiting to untangle","waiting to be untangled","that waited to untangling","for them to be untangled"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"체스 게임을 보면서 ‘(얽힌 것이) 풀리기를 기다리는’ 정교한 비밀이 있는 듯했다고 말한다. 빈 칸은 ‘비밀’을 꾸며주는 부분이므로 ‘(that were) waiting to be untangled’가 되어야 한다. 사람이 푸는 것이므로 비밀 입장에서는 ‘풀리다’라는 수동이 되어야 한다. 그러므로 정답은 ②번이다."},{"q":22,"stem":"Imagine that a drug company experiments with a plant that’s believed to inhibit the action of a virus. But nothing happens. It turns out that they picked the wrong sub-species of the plant, or they picked it at the wrong time of day. The plant chemicals can be different in the morning than they are at night. Or maybe the plants were old instead of young. All of these _____________ can make a difference.","opts":["indices","variables","facilitators","implications"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"제약회사가 약효를 가진 식물로 실험할 때 생기는 여러 가지 변수(variable)에 대한 내용이다. 빈칸 앞의 다양한 사례들은 변수에 따라 약효가 달라지는 보기들이다."},{"q":23,"stem":"Which species would you want to protect first, a tiger cub or a sloth? A panda or a frog? When it comes to an emotional response, the cuter creatures get more attention. They also get more research funding, global popularity, and conservation support. If you’re an animal, the fluffier your fur and the bigger your eyes, the better your chances for protection. That is, ___________ zoologist Lucy Cooke has a vote. She’s on a mission to show the world why some of the most unlovable animals are actually the most interesting and why they deserve our attentionㅡand our protection.","opts":["if","what","as","unless"],"pts":3.0,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":4,"ex":"‘루시 쿡이라는 동물학자가 투표권을 행사하지 않는다면’ 이라는 뜻이 되어야 하므로 정답은 ④번이다. 루시 쿡은 ‘가장 사랑스럽지 못한 동물들도 사실은 가장 흥미롭고 또 주목과 보호를 받을 만한 동물들임을’ 세상에 보여주는 것을 임무로 하기 때문이다."},{"q":24,"stem":"There are hundreds of studies on the effects of drinking coffee, but the results are often __________________. Some studies claim that consumption of coffee may lead to a higher risk of bladder and lung cancer, while some claim that it can reduce the risk of other cancers.","opts":["persistent","measurable","contradictory","interchangeable"],"pts":2.0,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"빈칸 다음의 내용을 보면 일부는 커피가 암의 위험을 높인다고 하고, 또 일부는 암의 위험을 줄여준다는 주장을하고 있으므로 빈칸에는 ‘상충하는’을 뜻하는 contradictory가 적절하다."},{"q":25,"stem":"In his early stages as a film director, Bong received a meager salary of US $1,900 per year and had to borrow rice from his friends. He became known to audiences and achieved a cult with his directorial debut film, the black comedy Barking Dogs Never Bite (2000) before ___________________ with his subsequent films, all of which are among the highest-grossing films in South Korea.","opts":["gaining critical acclaim","starting to connect the dots","turning his back on Hollywood","finding himself at the crossroads"],"pts":2.0,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"봉준호 감독의 초기 활동에 대한 내용으로, 2000년도의 <플란다스의 개(Barking Dogs Never Bite)>이후 비평적으로 인정을 받기 시작하는 부분에 대해 추론하도록하는 문제이다. ① gain critical acclaim은 ‘비평계의 갈채를 얻다, 호평을 받다’라는 의미이다."},{"q":26,"stem":"Which is true according to the above passage?","opts":["Ten years have passed since the last train of the High Line was operated.","One lack of the High Line is beautiful landscape, which is screened by tall buildings.","You can walk five times faster on the High Line than you would down on the ground.","It is more than twenty years since the High Line functioned as a popular spot for tourists."],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":0,"a":3,"ex":"하이라인 위에서는 건널목이나 신호등이 없으므로 아래에서 두 블록을 걸을 시간에 열 블록을 걸을 수 있다고 본문에서 말하므로, 옳은 것은 ③번이다. 마지막 열차의 운행 이후 (10년이 아니라) 20년이 지났고, 하이라인에서도 허드슨강의 아름다운 광 경을 볼 수 있으며, 유명 관광지가 된 것은 2009년부터이므로 20년이 아직 안 되었다."},{"q":27,"stem":"Choose the most suitable position of the sentence below in the above passage. By the time someone saw the labs, it was too late.","opts":["(A)","(B)","(C)","(D)"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":1,"a":4,"ex":"‘실험실의 테스트 결과들을 누군가가 보았을 즈음에는 이미 너무 늦었다’는 문장이 들어갈 곳은 보기 중에 마지막인 (D)이다. 그 바로 앞 문장에서 ‘누군가가 마침내 독성 테스트를 의뢰했다’고 하기 때문이다."},{"q":28,"stem":"From the passage, it can be inferred that _______________ committed an act of Internet fraud.","opts":["Jane","Wendy","Jane’s mother","Wendy’s mother"],"pts":2.0,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":2,"a":4,"ex":"대기자 명단에서 아래에 있던 웬디의 엄마가 그 앞에 있던 제인의 엄마 이름으로 계 정을 만들어 ‘명단에서 제인을 빼 달라’고 요구하는 이메일을 학교에 보낸다. 그 결과 웬디가 올라가게 된다. 그러므로 ‘인터넷 사기’를 저지른 사람은 ④번 웬디의 엄마이다."},{"q":29,"stem":"Which is implied in the passage?","opts":["Korean businesses have always been open to outsiders and foreign ideas.","The 1997 financial crisis helped Korean businesses to be competitive on a global scale.","Korean government was favorable especially to banking corporations before 1997.","Korean government forced big companies to be more innovative even before the crisis."],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":3,"a":2,"ex":"이 글의 내용은 1997년의 경제 위기 이전에는 한국의 정부, 금융, 기업이 서로 얽혀 있었으나 위기를 겪으면서 국제적인 경쟁에 노출되고 결과적으로는 더 혁신적이 되었 다는 것이다. 이런 내용과 가장 가까운 답안은 ②이다."},{"q":30,"stem":"Which lesson is implied in the passage?","opts":["Challenge all assumptions.","Constantly improve your ideas.","Record every idea and thought.","Turn your deficiencies to your advantage."],"pts":2.0,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":4,"a":4,"ex":"귀가 잘 안 들려서 오히려 주변 소음에 신경 쓰지 않고 자신의 일(다루던 도구)에 집중할 수 있었다는 에디슨에 관한 글이다. 귀가 잘 안 들린 덕분에 생각에 집중할 수 있었다고 믿어서, 에디슨은 청력장애인들을 위한 도구를 만들어달라는 요구를 거 절했다는 것이다. 그러므로 이 일화에 암시된 교훈은 ‘너의 결함을 이점으로 바꿔라’ 라는 ④번이다."},{"q":31,"stem":"Which is the best title of the passage?","opts":["The Value of Slow Reading","The Advance of the Digital World","Pros and Cons of Virtual Experience","The Importance of Privacy in the Digital World"],"pts":3.0,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":5,"a":4,"ex":"이 글은 디지털 시대에는 자아를 개발할 privacy (사적 공간, 자유)가 필요하다는 것을 강조한다. 따라서 제목으로 가장 적절한 것은 ④디지털 시대 사적 공간의 중요성이다. 천천히 진지하게 읽기의 가치를 논하고 있기는 하지만 그것은 자아를 발전시킬 수 있는 하나의 활동으로 제시한다. 따라서 ①보다는 ④가 글의 제목으로 더 적합하다."},{"q":32,"stem":"Which is the most appropriate proverb to describe the underlined part?","opts":["One good turn deserves another.","You can’t have a cake and eat it.","High buildings have low foundations.","Everybody’s business is nobody’s business."],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":6,"a":2,"ex":"소금과 다른 물질들 덕분으로 한겨울에도 신선한 야채를 먹는다든가 입천장에 달라 붙지 않는 땅콩버터, 균일하게 쌓아올려지는 감자칩 등을 먹을 수 있는데, 이러한 장 점들에도 불구하고 ‘무엇에든 대가가 있는 법’이어서 야채와 과일들의 경우에는 ‘맛’ 을 대가로 치른다는 이야기이다. ‘무엇에든 대가가 있는 법’을 뜻하는 속담은 ‘케이크를 가지고 있으면서 동시에 먹을 수는 없다’ 의 ②번이다."},{"q":33,"stem":"Which helped scientists discover how Beethoven died?","opts":["large amounts of lead in his blood","special tests they were recently able to do","some of Beethoven’s hair and bits of his skull","all the medical treatments he had during his life"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":7,"a":2,"ex":"이 글의 두 번째 문장은 과학자들이 서반구에서 가장 강력한 엑스레이 광선을 베토 벤의 신체 일부에 사용하여 그가 납 중독으로 죽었다는 사실을 밝혔다고 설명한다. 또한 다음 문장에서 이 결과가 과학자들을 흥분시킨 것은 그것이 더 먼저 나온 암시 나 단서들을 확인하기 때문이라고 한다. 이런 내용에 비추어볼 때 과학자들이 베토벤이 어떻게 죽었는지를 밝히는데 도움을 준 것은 “그들이 새롭게 사용할 수 있게 된 특별한 실험들”이라고 할 수 있다."},{"q":34,"stem":"Which is NOT suggested about a “set point”?","opts":["It controls body weight to stay within a certain range.","It is an ideal body weight range for each person.","It is not likely to be influenced by sudden input of food.","It helps the body fight back to defend its comfortable weight during a diet."],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":8,"a":2,"ex":"인체에 내재된 설정 값(set point)에 대해 설명하는 글이다. 이 때문에 음식섭취를 갑자기 늘이거나 줄이더라도 인체는 체중을 10-20퍼센트 이내 일정한 범위 안에서 유지하려고 한다(①)는 내용이다. 따라서 다이어트 중에도 체중이 쉽게 줄지 않는 이 유(③, ④)도 설명해준다. ② ‘이상적인 체중범위‘라는 표현은 본문에서 set point의 설명으로 나오지 않는다."},{"q":35,"stem":"Which is the most suitable for the blank?","opts":["Most of the energy they burn is from their resting metabolism.","It is the chemical reactions in the body's cells that change food and drink into energy.","In other words, the amount of calories they eat are equal to the amount they burn in one day.","A striking feature of metabolism is the similarity of the basic metabolic pathways among vastly different species."],"pts":3.0,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":8,"a":3,"ex":"빈칸의 앞부분은 ’신진대사(metabolism)가 음식섭취로 만들어내는 에너지와 일하는 데 사용하는 에너지의 밸런스를 맞춘다는 부분이므로 빈칸에는 ③ ‘다시 말하자면 흡 입한 칼로리와 사용한 칼로리가 같다’는 내용으로 유추할 수 있다. ① ‘대부분의 사용한 칼로리는 ’resting metabolism(휴지기의 신진대사)‘에서 나온다’는 내용이므로 답이 될 수 없다."},{"q":36,"stem":"Which is emphasized in the above passage?","opts":["The necessity of finding cures for new threatening diseases","The importance of psychosocial factors in determining longevity","The unexpected surprises concerning the study on the longevity","The importance of self-sufficiency in the matter of longevity"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":9,"a":2,"ex":"장수는 신체적 건강의 결과이기만 한 것이 아니고, 일상생활을 구성하며 거기에 영 향을 주는 모든 다양한 요인들 역시 중요함을 강조한 글이다. 즉, 이 글에서 강조하는 것은 ②번의 ‘장수를 결정하는 데 있어서의 사회 심리학적 요인들의 중요성’ 이다."},{"q":37,"stem":"Which is the most suitable for the blank?","opts":["calling off","falling off","putting off","staving off"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":9,"a":4,"ex":"빈 칸에 적당한 것은 ‘비키다, 회피하다’를 뜻하는 ④번 ‘staving off’ 이다. ‘call off (약속을 취소하다)’, ‘fall off (이탈하여 떨어지다)’, ‘put off (연기하다, 늦추다)’는 답으로 적합하지 않다."},{"q":38,"stem":"Choose the appropriate order of the paragraphs.","opts":["(A) - (B) - (C)","(A) - (C) - (B)","(B) - (C) - (A)","(C) - (A) - (B)"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":10,"a":2,"ex":"이 글은 코로나19 감염병 시대에 대중이 예술을 즐기는 방법과 어린이를 위한 예술 교육의 일환으로 mural(벽화)작업을 들고 있다. 따라서 이 글의 올바른 순서로는 (A) 감염병으로 인한 미술관 방문의 어려움—공공예술로서의 벽화제시 (C) 어린이 예술교 육의 사례로서의 벽화작업 (B) 감염병 시대의 새로운 벽화작업과 어린이 교육프로그 램의 중요성으로 결론지어지는 (A) - (C) - (B) 순서가 가장 자연스럽다."},{"q":39,"stem":"According to the passage, murals ______________.","opts":["need to be collaborated","should work like a big puzzle","are crucial in the difficult times","set artists free from social barriers"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":10,"a":1,"ex":"본문 중 (B)에 따르면 벽화란 함께 하는 작업인데 감염병으로 인해 따로 작업한 이 후 나중에 함께 붙인다는 내용이 있으므로 답은 ① ‘협력할 필요가 있다’가 된다. ② ‘항상 큰 퍼즐처럼 작용해야 한다’는 내용은 본문의 내용 (개인작업 이후 큰 퍼즐처 럼 나중에 맞추는 작업)에서 지나치게 많이 비약한 선택지이다."},{"q":40,"stem":"Which is the best title of the passage?","opts":["Helping Children with Art Programs","The Importance of Art in the Community","How to Be Creative in the COVID-19 Era","Working on the Murals during the Pandemic"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":10,"a":4,"ex":"이 글은 코로나 19 시대 예술, 특히 벽화작업에 관해 다루고 있으므로 가장 적절한 제목은 ④ ‘팬데믹 시대의 벽화작업’이 적절하다. ①, ②는 본문의 주제를 일부만 담고 있으므로 제목으로 적절하지 않다."}]},"2023":{"sections":["Choose the one that is closest in meaning to the underlined word(s).","Choose the one that best fills in the blank.","Choose the one that most grammatically completes the sentence.","Choose the one that is grammatically INCORRECT.","Choose the one(s) that best complete(s) the sentence.","Read the following passages and answer the questions."],"passages":["Sand dunes are hills of sand. They are formed by the build-up of small particles of sand that are moved by the wind. They can have a wide variety of shapes and sizes, depending upon the intensity and direction of the wind. Contrary to popular opinion, dunes play an important role in ecology. They can be home to unique plants and animals. In addition, they may serve as wind breaks and protect areas further inland. For these reasons, many governments are now starting to protect sand dunes since human development can easily damage the fragile structures.","In 1963, in the unremarkable seaside town of La Coruña, Spain, 27-year-old Amancio Ortega Gaona started a business making bathrobes. By 1975, Ortega had saved enough money from this business to open a clothing store in town. He named his store Zorba, after Zorba the Greek. However, he soon learned that there was a bar in town called Zorba just a couple of blocks away. The bar owner thought that it might be confusing to have two businesses in town with the same name, so Ortega agreed to change the name of his store. The problem was that he had already made the letter molds for the store’s sign. Rather than having new molds made, Ortega used some of the letters he already had molds for, and came up with a new name: Zara.","Native people create legends to explain unusual phenomena in their environment. A legend from the Hawaiian island of Kauai explains how the naupaka flower, a flower that grows on beaches there, got its unusual shape. (A) The flower looks like half a small daisy—there are petals on one side only. (B) The legend says that the marriage of two young lovers on the island was opposed by both sets of parents. (C) The parents found the couple together on a beach one day, and to prevent them from being together, one of the families moved to the mountains, separating the young couple forever. (D) One half moved to the mountains, and the other half stayed near the beach. This story is a good example of a legend invented by native people to interpret the world around them.","Ballet is a dance form which utilizes specific techniques and methods to achieve a motion that is graceful, flowing, and precise. The line of a dancer’s body is crucial in that whether the body is resting or moving, its different parts have to be in complete harmony. The different techniques are choreographed into an orchestral, operatic, or balletic work. Before ballet’s traditions developed, narrative dance began and evolved in countries as diverse as China, India, and ancient Greece. The Roman Empire integrated Greek dance after conquering Greece, and by the 1400s, the first glimmers of ballet began to emerge in Italy. Domenico da Piacenza, one of the first dance masters, was in charge of teaching nobles the art; Fabritio Caroso’s publication Il Ballarino, a manual on the technical aspects of the dance, played a role in establishing Italy as the center of technical ballet development.","Fragmentation allows for multiple offsprings to be created at the same time. Planarians, a type of flatworm, will break up into multiple pieces when they reproduce. Each piece will grow and develop into a complete new worm. Up to eight or nine new planarians can be created from a single parent. They also have the ability to regenerate. They can re-grow their entire body even if there is less than one percent of the original.","Distance learning is heavily dependent on technology, particularly the Internet. On a face-to-face course, students may only require a computer for the purpose of writing an essay. In comparison, when learning remotely, technology is the principal means of communication. The flexibility this provides means that students may be better able to learn at their own pace, following their own timetable, but it may also mean that learners have to be well-organized and self-disciplined. They must therefore be highly motivated in order to do well on the distance-learning courses.","","What is sound? As an object vibrates in space, it imparts some of its energy to the surrounding molecules. This energy makes one group of molecules crowd together and a separate group disperse. The former process is called condensation, and the latter rarefaction. Together, these two processes form a sound wave. All objects that vibrate produce sound waves. The waves transmit their energy to other molecules farther away. This process continues until the total energy of the wave disappears. As the wave travels through the air, it causes a change in air pressure known as sound pressure.","America had fulfilled my ambition. I had arrived with the equivalent of a high school diploma, and after 10 years, I hold a graduate degree and have a relatively successful professional career. That is not to say it had been easy. Every inch of progress had been achieved through exhausting battles. My college education had been financed partly through working multiple minimum-wage jobs. Upon graduation, I had gotten a job, but adjusting to corporate culture was initially very difficult. Then, nervous about job security, I went to graduate school part time to give myself a(n) _____ in case of job layoffs. And I had spent a small fortune in legal fees and had endured many stressful years for the sake of becoming a permanent resident in America.","Two of the major theories of crime that have come from structural functionalism are \"strain theory\" and \"control theory.\" Strain theory was developed by Robert Merton. It uses Durkheim's concept of anomie: the absence of norms to guide people's behavior. Merton argued that when the structure of society doesn't permit people to reach their goals (such as obtaining enough money to live on), the strain (or tension) that results may lead to crime. Society encourages everyone to want the same things (a job, money), but doesn't provide opportunities for everyone. Strain theory explains criminal behavior as a result of blocked opportunities. However, if blocked opportunities are responsible for crime, why don't more people become criminals? Control theory may answer that question. Hirschi (1996) suggests that strong social bonds prevent people from violating social norms or rules. A crucial aspect of these social ties is (A) to other people. Ford (2005) concludes that a strong family bond (B) the likelihood of substance abuse and criminal behavior among young people.","(A) Americans dislike government interference in their private lives, but they might agree to a tax if they had to pay higher taxes. Today, the annual cost of obesity-related health care in the United States is estimated by some researchers to be $190 billion, or 20 percent of the total health care costs in the country. It is expected to almost double by 2030. It won't be long before there are more and more people saying: \"Why didn't the government do more to combat this crisis?\" (B) The bigger question is whether a tax like this one would be politically acceptable. Probably not― because Americans traditionally don't like the government to interfere in their private lives. One example is the unsuccessful attempt to ban oversized sodas in New York City restaurants. The public was outraged. \"We don't like being bossed around by the government,\" residents said. \"This is becoming a nanny state,\" they argued. In fact, a poll by NBC found that as many as 6 in 10 New Yorkers felt that the ban was a bad idea. Similarly, an April 2012 national survey on a related topic found that only 26 percent of Americans said that they would support taxing high-fat and high-sugar food. (C) Would a tax on unhealthy foods be effective? Absolutely. First, we have a history of successfully discouraging unhealthy habits by putting a high price tag on them. For instance, high taxes on tobacco worked to reduce the number of smokers in the United States. People were less likely to buy cigarettes―or simply bought fewer than usual―because they did not want to spend more money on them. It seems likely that our food habits would change just as our cigarette habits did. Second, research shows that if a tax of 18 percent were put on soda and pizza alone, the average American could lose five pounds."],"questions":[{"q":1,"stem":"I saw that the best thing I could do was get hold of a dictionary to study and learn some words.","opts":["analyze","publish","obtain","discard"],"pts":2.0,"inline":false,"sec":0,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"get hold of는 ‘얻다, 구하다’란 뜻이므로 동일한 의미를 가진 ③obtain(획득하다)이 정답이다."},{"q":2,"stem":"Current squad of South Korea has little resemblance of its 2002 version led by Guus Hiddink which intrigued fans with its audacious style and resilience.","opts":["vicious","inordinate","fearless","elusive"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":0,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"audacious는 ‘대담한, 용기있는’의 의미를 가진 형용사이다. 보기에 나온 단어들 중에 ‘용맹한’의 의미를 가진 ③fearless가 audacious와 가장 유사하다."},{"q":3,"stem":"The negative effect of social media on our ability to focus on work is significant and should not be dismissed.","opts":["discharged","discounted","deteriorated","dwindled"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":0,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"dismissed는 ‘(고려할 가치가 없다고) 묵살하다’라는 의미로 이와 유사한 뜻을 가진 ②discounted(무시하다)가 정답이다."},{"q":4,"stem":"Juggling two languages in the brain probably leads to advantages for bilinguals. Still, researchers emphasize, this doesn't mean they learn better than monolinguals. However, it does keep the brain more nimble.","opts":["agile","vigilant","tenacious","stringent"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":0,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"nimble은 ‘생각이 민첩한, 영리한’이란 뜻이므로 동일한 의미를 가진 ①agile(기민한)이 정답이다."},{"q":5,"stem":"Kevin’s Pulitzer Prize-winning photograph of an emaciated Sudanese toddler being stalked by a vulture drew enormous response from readers and enormous interest in the plight of victims of famine.","opts":["anxious","desperate","gaunt","indigenous"],"pts":3.0,"inline":false,"sec":0,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"emaciated은 ‘여윈’, ’쇠약한’이란 의미의 형용사이다. 따라서 보기에 나온 단어들 가운데 ‘수척한’, ‘몹시 여윈’의 뜻을 갖는 ③gaunt가 가장 유사하다."},{"q":6,"stem":"In the spring, almost all woodchuck’s body fat has been used up to keep it alive during its long sleep. By February or March, the _________ animal is ready to leave its hole and go looking for its first meal.","opts":["famished","capricious","attentive","rampant"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":1,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"Woodchuck은 긴 겨울잠을 자면서 몸에 비축했던 지방을 다 써버린다. 그래서 2~3 월에 첫 식사를 할 때 ‘굶주린, 몹시 배고픈’ 상태이기 때문에 ①famished가 적절하다."},{"q":7,"stem":"The ____________ leadership resulted in the terrible accident that took the lives of many innocent people.","opts":["blundering","mighty","tolerant","propitious"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":1,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"‘(어리석은) 실수를 저지르는’ 정부가 결국 무고한 많은 이들의 목숨을 앗아간 끔찍한 사고를 낳게 되었다는 내용이므로 ①blundering이 가장 적절하다."},{"q":8,"stem":"Buy Nothing Day is scheduled each year to take place in late November so that it ________________ the beginning of the busiest shopping period of the year in North America―the month leading up to Christmas day.","opts":["accounts for","refers to","coincides with","engages in"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":1,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"Buy Nothing Day는 크리스마스로 이어지는 북미에서 가장 쇼핑을 많이 하기 시작하는 11월 말에 맞추어 열린다는 내용이므로 정답은 ‘(동시에) 일어나다’의 뜻을 가 진 ③coincides with이다."},{"q":9,"stem":"often travelers experience bad service from the bus company, they continue to use it because of the low fare.","opts":["Whenever","How","However","When"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"[however + 형용사[or 부사] + 주어 + 동사]의 어순을 묻는 문제이다. 버스 회사의 형편없는 서비스를 ‘아무리 자주’ 경험한다고 하더라도, 저렴한 요금 때문에 여행 자들은 계속 그 버스를 이용한다는 내용이다."},{"q":10,"stem":"Not until I came across a report on sleep deprivation ______________________ something was wrong.","opts":["I finally found out","had I finally found out","did I finally find out","I had finally found out"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"강조를 위해 not until 절(또는 구)이 문두에 나오면 그 뒤에 오는 절은 도치가 된다. 따라서 주어와 동사가 도치되어서 did I finally find out이 된다."},{"q":11,"stem":"As climate change leads to higher temperatures around the world, mosquitoes are now able to survive in areas for them.","opts":["when they are once so cold","which they were once so cold","where were once too cold","that were once too cold"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":4,"ex":"‘areas’를 선행사로 받는 (주격) 관계사절을 찾는 문제이다. 과거(once)에 모기들에 게는 ‘지나치게’(‘too’, 부정적이거나 무언가가 원하는 한계를 초과하는) 추웠던(추워서 생존할 수 없었던) 지역에서 모기들이 지금은 살아남을 수 있다‘는 내용이므로 ④ that were once too cold가 정답이다."},{"q":12,"stem":"Over the past few years, the number of wildfires around the world, especially in countries with large forests.","opts":["was increased","has increased","were increasing","have been increasing"],"pts":2.0,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"단수 주어인 ‘the number’는 단수 동사가 필요하고 ’over the past few years’(지난 몇 년에 걸쳐서)는 현재완료 시제를 요구한다. 따라서 수(일치)와 시제를 맞춘 ②has increased가 정답이다."},{"q":13,"stem":"One marine life form divers should only observe from a distance is the sea snake. They are not usually aggressive but may become so _________.","opts":["if disturbed","when disturbing","for disturbance","to disturb"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"물뱀은 ‘방해를 받으면 공격적으로 바뀔 수도 있다’는 의미이므로 수동의 의미를 가 진 ①if disturbed가 정답이다. If they are disturbed에서 주어와 동사(they are)가 생 략된 구조이다."},{"q":14,"stem":"In the past, students had to visit colleges to see _____________, but today many colleges let you explore their campuses online.","opts":["what they were looked","what they looked like","how they were looked","how they looked like"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"과거에는 ‘캠퍼스가 어떻게 생겼는지 보려면 직접 학교를 방문해야 했었다’는 내용이다. look은 자동사이고 what은 like와 함께 쓰여야 ‘~하게(~처럼) 보인다’는 의미이므로 정답은 ②what they looked like이다."},{"q":15,"stem":"In England, landlords and businessmen who had any surplus money began to deposit it for safety with the goldsmith. And he would lend the money ①at a high interest. Gradually his lending department became so profitable that he stopped ②charging the depositors for safeguarding their wealth, and he actually paid them for doing it. He would of course pay them less than he charged those ③borrowed from him. The difference between what he paid depositors and what he charged borrowers ④constituted his profits. The modern bank has shed its goldsmith’s business and has specialized in this receiving and loaning of money.","opts":["at a","charging the","borrowed from","constituted his"],"pts":2.5,"inline":true,"sec":3,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"사람들(those)이 goldsmith로부터 돈을 빌리는 주체이므로 ③borrowed를 현재분사 인 borrowing으로 바꿔야 한다."},{"q":16,"stem":"An eclipse occurs when a celestial object passes between two others. The most commonly observed from the Earth ①is solar and lunar eclipses. Solar eclipses are when the moon passes between the sun and the Earth. The moon may appear to be ②nearly the same size as the sun since the moon is much ③closer to the Earth. This results in the moon partially or completely ④blocking out the sun. A lunar eclipse is when the moon passes through the Earth's shadow. As the moon passes behind the Earth, it either darkens or disappears.","opts":["is solar","nearly the","closer to","blocking out"],"pts":3.0,"inline":true,"sec":3,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"한 천체가 다른 두 개의 천체 사이를 통과할 때 일어나는 eclipse(식)를 설명하는 내용이다. Solar and lunar eclipses are the most commonly observed from the Earth라는 문장에서 주어와 동사의 위치가 도치된 구문으로 주어가 복수이므로 동사는 are로 고쳐야 한다."},{"q":17,"stem":"Did you ever have that sensation where you’re watching someone do something―serve a tennis ball, say, or get pricked by a needle―and you can just feel exactly what they must be feeling, as if you were in their shoes? Scientists have long wondered why we get that feeling, and more than two decades ago, a team of Italian researchers thought they (A) on an answer. While observing monkeys’ brains, they noticed that certain cells activated both when a monkey performed an action and when that monkey (B) another monkey perform the same action. “Mirror neurons” were discovered.","opts":["(A) stumbled (B) watched","(A) brought (B) heard","(A) dwelt (B) made","(A) lingered (B) let"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"우리가 다른 사람의 어떤 행위를 보면서 왜 그와 동일한 경험을 하게 되는지에 대한 의문에 대해 이탈리아 연구자들이 그 해답을 발견한 것 같다는 내용이다. 따라서 (A) 에는 다른 표현은 적절하지 않고 ‘우연히 발견하다’는 뜻의 stumbled (on)이 들어가 야 한다. 또한, 한 원숭이가 자신이 했던 행동을 다른 원숭이가 동일하게 하는 것을 ‘볼 때’ 그 원숭이의 특정 세포들이 활성화되는 것을 목격했다는 내용이므로 (B)에는 watched가 적절하다."},{"q":18,"stem":"A tunicate bulb may be identified by its thin paper-like covering, which serves to protect the bulb from drying out or becoming injured. Tulips, daffodils, and hyacinths are examples of tunicate bulbs. For many of the tunicates, new bulbs form around the original bulb. Called offset, these new bulbs sprout from the base of the main bulb and begin to grow completely new plants. Soon, however, these plants begin crowding each other out, with the result that the flowers begin to shrink in size. Once this happens, to ensure their continued survival, they need to be .","opts":["more fertilized","watered more often","manually separated","exposed to the sun"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"분지(offset)라 불리는 새 구근(bulb)들이 main bulb에서 나와서 완전히 새로운 plants로 자란다. 이 plants가 지나치게 많아지면서 결국 꽃의 사이즈가 쪼그라들고 마는데, 일단 이런 일이 발생하면 plants를 일일이 ‘손으로 분리시켜 주어야’ 이것들이 계속 살아남을 수 있다는 내용이다. 따라서 ③manually separated가 정답이다."},{"q":19,"stem":"For weeks, I had been traveling through some of the best tiger habitats in Asia, but never before had I seen a tiger. Partly this was because of the animal’s legendarily nature. The tiger is powerful enough to kill and drag prey five times its weight, yet it can move through high grass, forest, and even water in unnerving silence. Those who have witnessed―or survived―an attack commonly report that the tiger “came from nowhere.”","opts":["untenable","threatening","lethal","secretive"],"pts":2.0,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":4,"ex":"아시아의 최대 호랑이 서식지를 돌아다녀도 한 마리도 보지 못했던 것은 호랑이의 ‘무서우리만치 조용하게,’ ‘갑자기 모습을 드러내는’ ‘비밀스러운’ 성향 때문이다. 따 라서 빈칸에는 untenable(지지할 수 없는). threatening(위협적인), lethal(치명적인)보다 ④secretive가 더 적절하다."},{"q":20,"stem":"Ants are known to be amazing collaborators―they work together to build homes, find food, and fight off their enemies. But perhaps one of the most astounding examples of ant teamwork is the (A) way that fire ants are able to cope with flooding. If their home is flooded, fire ants will join themselves together, gripping tight with their jaws and legs, to form a pizza-like shape that can float on water like a raft. Some rafts can last up to three weeks, and it is thought that some of the bigger structures may have more than 100,000 ants. But if you see one, stay well clear. Fire ants have a painful sting and are thought to be even more (B) than usual when in a raft formation.","opts":["(A) complementary (B) intricate","(A) ingenious (B) aggressive","(A) unpredictable (B) repellent","(A) versatile (B) competitive"],"pts":3.0,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"개미들의 팀워크를 보여주는 놀라운 예로 홍수에 대처하는 불개미들의 ‘기발한, 독 창적인’(ingenious) 방법을 설명하고 있다. stay well clear(멀리 떨어져 있어라)는 표 현에서 알 수 있듯이 불개미들이 뗏목(raft)의 형태를 하고 있을 때 더 ‘공격적’(aggressive)인 상태가 된다는 것을 알 수 있다."},{"q":21,"stem":"Nuclear power is often used to generate electricity for twenty-first century needs. It is produced for this purpose by commercial nuclear reactors in nuclear power plants. In general, these reactors are reliable and efficient. (A) , dangerous accidents or other serious problems can occur, so nuclear reactors must be built to withstand everything from hurricanes to terrorist attacks. (B) , these safety measures are not always adequate. Shortly after an earthquake hit Japan on March 11, 2011, a chain of events led to explosions at the Fukushima Daiichi nuclear plant.","opts":["(A) Still (B) Unfortunately","(A) In addition (B) Therefore","(A) In fact (B) Nevertheless","(A) However (B) Furthermore"],"pts":2.0,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"‘일반적으로 핵 원자로들은 믿을 수 있고 효율적이다’는 내용 뒤에 ‘위험한 사고나 기타 심각한 문제들이 발생할 수 있다는 상반된 내용이 나온다. 따라서 (A)에는 ’그 럼에도, 그러나‘의 의미를 지닌 Still을 쓰는 게 어울린다. 이들 원자로가 허리케인에서 테러리스트의 공격에 이르기까지 모든 것을 견딜 수 있도록 만들어져야만 한다는 (B)의 앞 내용과 ’이들 안전 조치들이 항상(언제나) 적절한 것은 아니다‘라는 뒤의 내 용을 연결시키기 위해 가장 적절한 것은 ‘불행하게도’(Unfortunately)이다."},{"q":22,"stem":"There are both benefits and risks attached to a government that tries to control the safety of its citizens. This can reduce accidents, disease and crime, and (A) for the basic needs of all members of society. Conversely, however, over-protective legislation can limit individual freedom and cause (B) . It can also suggest that people do not have to be responsible for their own actions.","opts":["(A) apply (B) trouble","(A) cater (B) resentment","(A) arrange (B) detention","(A) settle (B) indulgence"],"pts":3.0,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"시민들의 안전을 위해 정부가 통제권을 행사할 때 야기되는 이점 및 우려를 다룬 내 용이다. 사고, 질병, 범죄를 줄여주고 사회구성원의 기본 요구를 충족해준다는 이점이 있지만, 개인의 자유를 제한하여 분노를 일으킬 수 있다는 점이 우려된다는 면에서 빈칸에는 각각 ‘(요구)~에 응하다, 충족하다’의 의미인 (A)cater for와 ‘분노’의 의미 인 (B)resentment가 들어가야 한다."},{"q":23,"stem":"The most popular cell phone activity is taking pictures. Among all cell phone users, 82% use their phone to take photos. There is (A) difference between males and females. For instance, 82% of men and 81% of women take pictures with their phones. (B) , young adults are the most likely to take pictures. Ninety-four percent of those under 29 take pictures with their cell phones, compared to just 44% of those aged 65 and over.","opts":["(A) some (B) Quite unexpectedly","(A) one (B) Most importantly","(A) few (B) More than usually","(A) little (B) Perhaps unsurprisingly"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":4,"ex":"가장 자주 사용되는 휴대전화 기능은 사진 찍기이고 이를 남녀노소의 비율로 설명하는 글이다. 남녀비율 면에서 차이가 ‘거의 없다’는 의미를 담아서 불가산 명사를 수식할 수 있는 한정사는 (A)little이다. 그리고 장년층과 비교했을 때 젊은이들이 휴대전 화의 사진찍기 기능을 더 자주 사용할 것이라는 점은 예측 가능하다는 흐름으로 보아 (B)Perhaps unsurprisingly가 가장 적절하다."},{"q":24,"stem":"Psychologist Carol Dweck has conducted a series of studies showing the dangers of believing that geniuses are born rather than made. In one study, Dweck and researcher Valanne Henderson asked 229 seventh graders whether people are \"born smart\" or \"get smart\" by working hard. Then they compared the students' sixth and seventh grade achievement scores. The scores of students with the get-smart beliefs stayed high or improved. In contrast, the scores of students who believed in the born-smart assumption stayed low or declined. Surprisingly, even students who ______________________ but who had low confidence did very well. And the students whose scores dropped the most were the born-smart believers with high confidence.","opts":["believed in working hard","faced high expectations","worshiped their ability","made good grades"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"똑똑함은 타고난다고 믿을 때 뒤따르는 위험성을 보여주는 실험에 관한 글이다. 229명 학생들의 6학년과 7학년의 성적을 비교한 결과 똑똑함은 ‘노력해서 얻어진다 (get smart)’고 믿는 학생들의 성적이 가장 높았고, 반면에 ‘선천적으로 타고난다 (born smart)’고 확신있게 응답한 학생들의 성적은 가장 저조했다. 따라서 문맥상 이 런 ‘확신이 없더라도 get smart를 믿는 학생들의 성적이 우수하다’는 것을 유추할 수 있으므로 빈칸에는 ①believed in working hard가 들어가야 한다."},{"q":25,"stem":"Studies have shown that thinking about the way we eat food means we consume less. Mindless Eating author Brian Wansink conducted an experiment to show this. He gave stale popcorn to cinemagoers in different sizes. When he weighed the buckets after the film, he found those with bigger buckets ate 53 percent more. When we don't make a conscious decision to think about food, ______________________________.","opts":["we are more likely to be fooled by cinema marketing strategy","the chemicals that tell our brain we're full never work","we will eat anything and we eat more of it and get fatter.","the people who have more options eat more"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"음식에 대한 사고와 음식 소비량이 관련이 있다는 사실이 실험을 통해 입증되었다는 내용이다. 영화 관람객에게 신선하지 않은 팝콘을 제공한 후 소비량을 측정하였는데, 큰 용기(bucket)에 담아 제공된 음식의 소비량이 훨씬 많은 것을 알 수 있었다. 따라서 ‘음식에 대해 의식적으로 생각하지 않으면 아무 음식이나 많이 먹게된다’는 내용이 어울리므로 빈칸에는 ③이 들어가야 한다."},{"q":26,"stem":"According to the passage, sand dunes _________.","opts":["consist of many layers of soil blown from the hills","provide a habitat for specific vegetation and wildlife","act as a natural barrier against the sun rays","can be facilitated by human interference"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":0,"a":2,"ex":"모래언덕의 형성과 역할에 대해 설명하는 글이다. ①,③,④는 글의 내용과 다르고 ‘모래언덕은 특정 식물과 야생생물의 서식지가 될 수 있다’는 내용이 언급되었으므로 ②가 정답이다."},{"q":27,"stem":"Which is the best title of the passage?","opts":["Success of an Entrepreneur","Popularity of Zorba the Greek","Importance of Brand Naming","Birth of a Brand"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":1,"a":4,"ex":"사업으로 돈을 많이 번 스페인의 한 사업가가 옷 가게를 열면서 소설 제목인 ‘그리 스인, 조르바’를 따라 상호명을 Zorba로 정한다. 하지만 이미 근처에 Zorba라는 술집이 있다는 사실을 알고 상호명을 변경하기로 하는데, 이때 글자틀(molds)을 새로 만 들지 않고 이미 만들어 놓은 것들을 사용해서 Zara라는 명칭을 쓰기로 했다는 내용이다. 따라서 Zara라는 ‘브랜드가 탄생’하게 된 과정을 이야기이므로 ④가 제목으로 적절하다."},{"q":28,"stem":"Choose the most suitable position of the sentence below in the above passage. As the result, the naupaka flower separated itself into two halves.","opts":["(A)","(B)","(C)","(D)"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":2,"a":4,"ex":"하와이 원주민들은 특이한 현상을 전설로 설명한다. (A) 해변에서 자라는 naupaka 꽃은 한쪽에만 꽃잎이 있는 특이한 모양을 지니는데 (B), 전설에서 자식들의 결혼을 반대하던 부모님들은 (C) 해변가에서 발견된 그 커플이 헤어지도록, 한 가족은 산으로 이사하게 된다. (D)‘결과적으로 (커플처럼) naupaka 꽃은 두 부분으로 나뉘게 된다.’ (꽃의) 반은 산으로 가고, 나머지 반은 해변가에 남게 된다는 전설이다. 그러므로 인용한 예문은 한 가족이 산으로 이사한다는 얘기와 꽃의 반은 산으로, 나머지 반은 해변에 남게 된다는 얘기 사이의 위치인 ④ (D)가 적당하다."},{"q":29,"stem":"According to the passage, which is true?","opts":["The origin of ballet goes back to countries such as China and India.","Ballet in Italy began around the 15th century.","All the aristocrats in Italy took ballet lessons.","An instruction book on ballet technique had a great influence on many countries."],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":3,"a":2,"ex":"이탈리아에서 발레가 처음으로 등장하기 시작한 것은 1400년경이라는 내용이 나온다. 따라서 정답은 ②이다. Domenico da Piacenza가 귀족들(nobles)에게 춤을 가르 쳤다는 내용이 있긴 하지만, 모든 귀족들이 발레 수업을 받았다고 할 수는 없다. 발 레 테크닉에 대한 매뉴얼이 이탈리아에서 큰 역할을 했다는 내용은 있지만 이를 많은 나라로 확대해석할 수는 없다."},{"q":30,"stem":"Which is implied in the passage?","opts":["Fragmentation helps the organism evolve faster than in other ways.","Fragmentation makes the offsprings even stronger than the parent.","Planarians never succeed in finding a proper mate.","Planarians can regenerate the body when damaged."],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":4,"a":4,"ex":"무사분열(fragmentation)을 하는 플라나리아는 번식할 때 여러 개로 쪼개져 온전하게 새로운 개체가 된다. 이 새로운 개체는 몸체의 1퍼센트도 안되는 부분만 있어도 다시 자라나는 재생력이 있다는 내용이 나오므로 ④‘손상을 입어도 재생될 수 있다’ 가 정답이다."},{"q":31,"stem":"According to the passage, distance learning _____________________.","opts":["needs technological access","is limited by geography","lacks scheduling flexibility","suits all kinds of students"],"pts":2.0,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":5,"a":1,"ex":"원격 학습(distance learning)의 특징(인터넷 기술, 원거리 학습, 시간의 유연한 활 용, 학습자에게 요구되는 자세)을 설명하는 글이므로 ①이 정답이다."},{"q":32,"stem":"Language symbolizes reality; it’s not the reality itself. Of course, this is obvious. But consider: have you ever reacted to the way something was labeled or described rather than to the actual item? Have you ever bought something because of its name rather than because of the actual objects? If so, you were probably responding as if language was the reality, a distortion called intensional orientation. Intensional orientation refers to the tendency to view people, objects, and events in terms of how they are talked about or labeled rather than in terms of how they actually exist. It occurs when you act as if the words and labels are . 32. Which is the most suitable for the blank?","opts":["less realistic than the ideas they generate","more rational than the things they express","less complicated than the ideas they symbolize","more important than the things they represent"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":6,"a":4,"ex":"언어는 실재(reality)를 상징하지만, 실재 그 자체는 아니다. 이 글은 사람들이 언어가 실재인 것처럼 행동하는 양태를 분석하고 있다. ‘내재적 지향성’(intensional orientation)은 바로 이처럼 ‘사람, 사물, 그리고 사건을 그것들이 실제로 어떻게 존재 하느냐가 아니라 그것들이 어떻게 말해지거나 어떻게 라벨이 붙여지는지의 측면에서 바라보는 경향’을 일컫는다. ‘이것은 말과 라벨이 그것들이(words and labels) 나타 내는 것들(things)보다 더 중요한 것처럼 행동할 때 일어난다’는 내용이므로 ④가 정 답이다."},{"q":33,"stem":"Which is true about the movement of a sound wave?","opts":["It carries the sound energy in a vacuum.","It disturbs neighboring particles.","It will continue until it is blocked.","It becomes intense as it moves farther from the source."],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":7,"a":2,"ex":"소리와 그 특성에 관해 설명하는 글이다. 진동하는 모든 물체는 음파를 만들고 자신이 가진 에너지를 주변 분자들에게 전달하여 이 분자들을 밀집/분산시킨다. 또한 더 멀리 떨어진 분자들에게도 전달되며 이 과정은 파동의 전체 에너지가 사라질 때까지 계속된다는 내용이 나오므로 ②‘음파는 주변의 분자를 불안정하게 하다’가 정답이다."},{"q":34,"stem":"Which is the most suitable for the blank?","opts":["obsession","reward","edge","justification"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":8,"a":3,"ex":"글쓴이(나)가 직장을 잃을 경우에 대비해 ‘경쟁력’을 갖추고자 직장과 병행하면서 학 교를 졸업했다는 내용이다. 따라서 ‘유리한, 우위를 차지하는’을 뜻하는 ‘edge’가 정 답이다."},{"q":35,"stem":"Which is the best title of the passage?","opts":["The Way to Achieve Your Dreams","The Benefits of Education","Common Challenges of Working Students","An Immigrant's Silent Struggle"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":8,"a":4,"ex":"고등학교를 졸업하고 미국으로 온 후 역경을 딛고 묵묵하게 열심히 노력해서 자신의 야망을 이룬 이민자의 이야기를 다루고 있다. 따라서 적절한 제목은 ‘An Immigrant’s Silent Struggle’이다."},{"q":36,"stem":"Choose the one that best completes the blanks.","opts":["(A) spread (B) assesses","(A) visible (B) removes","(A) obedience (B) mitigates","(A) attachment (B) lowers"],"pts":3.0,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":9,"a":4,"ex":"두 가지 범죄이론, strain theory와 control theory에 관한 내용이다. 이 중 strain theory는 기회가 차단(박탈)될 때 범죄가 발생한다고 보고 있는데, 이때 더 많은 범죄 자가 나오지 않는 이유는 사회적 규범을 어기지 않게 만드는 사람들 간의 강력한 유 대 관계에 있다고 본다. 이 사회적 결속 관계의 중요한 한 양상이 다른 사람들에 대한 ‘애착관계’이며, 가족의 끈끈한 결속이 젊은이들의 약물중독과 범죄행위의 가능성을 ‘줄여준다’는 내용이므로 attachment (to)와 lowers가 정답이다."},{"q":37,"stem":"It can be inferred from the underlined part that __________________________.","opts":["social standards are not necessary for regulating behavior","people feel unstable when the society's values break down","people need not learn to distinguish right from wrong","a society lacking order encourages people to have the same goals"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":9,"a":2,"ex":"Durkheim은 아노미(anomie)의 개념을 사용해서 ‘사람들의 행동을 이끌어줄 규범의 부재’를 설명한다. 그러므로 여기에서 유추할 수 있는 사실은 ‘사회의 가치체계가 무 너질 때 사람들은 불안해한다’는 ②가 정답이다."},{"q":38,"stem":"Choose the appropriate order of the paragraphs.","opts":["(A) - (C) - (B)","(B) - (C) - (A)","(C) - (A) - (B)","(C) - (B) - (A)"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":10,"a":4,"ex":"(A)는 미국인들이 정부의 개입은 싫어하지만, 비만 관련 의료비용 부담이 늘고 있는 지금의 심각한 상황에서 이를 막을 수만 있다면 정부의 더 많을 역할을 기대하면서 더 많은 세금에 동의할 수도 있다는 내용이 나오고, (B)는 이런 세금이 정치적으로 합당한지 의문을 제기하면서, 미국인들은 전통적으로 정부가 사생활에 개입/간섭하는 것을 싫어한다는 내용이 나온다. 그리고 정부의 이런 조치에 뉴욕 시민들이 부정적으로 생각한다는 점을 설문조사 결과로 보여주고 있다. (C)에서는 건강을 해치는 음식에 관해 세금을 부과해야 한다는 저자의 강력한 주장을 담배에 부과된 세금의 성공적 인 사례를 들어 뒷받침하고 있다. 따라서 유해한 음식에 세금을 부과해야한다는 글쓴 이의 주장을 다룬 (C)가 가장 먼저 나오고, 이때 제기될 수 있는 세금부과에 대한 정 치적 문제 및 부정적 여론을 보여주는 (B)가 그 다음에 온다. 그러나 결국 사람들은 정부의 더 많은 역할을 요구하면서 기꺼이 세금을 더 낼 수도 있을 거라는 (A)가 마 지막에 오는 것이 문맥의 흐름상 가장 자연스럽다."},{"q":39,"stem":"What is the passage mainly about?","opts":["The problem of overweight and obesity","The crisis of the American health care system","The need to put a tax on unhealthy foods","The importance of the government intervention"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":10,"a":3,"ex":"건강을 해치는 음식에 대한 세금 부과의 필요성을 주장하는 내용이므로 정답은 ③이다."},{"q":40,"stem":"According to the passage, which is true?","opts":["The lack of health awareness is a significant problem for Americans.","It is inevitable that a decrease in tax is in America's future.","A poll in 2012 found that almost three-quarters of Americans would oppose the tax.","Smoking status and food habits are closely related."],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":10,"a":3,"ex":"26퍼센트의 미국인들이 고지방 고당분 음식에 세금을 부과하는 것에 반대한다는 설 문조사 결과 내용이 있으므로 ③이 정답이다. ①건강에 대한 인식 부족, ②앞으로 미 국에 세금 감소가 불가피할 것, ④흡연 유무와 음식 습관과의 관련성은 글의 내용과 관계가 없다."}]},"2024":{"sections":["Choose the one that is closest in meaning to the underlined word(s).","Choose the one that best fills in the blank.","Choose the one that most grammatically completes the sentence.","Choose the one that is grammatically INCORRECT.","Choose the one(s) that best complete(s) the sentence.","Read the following passages and answer the questions."],"passages":["Immortality has become commonplace. It has long departed the field of religion in which it appeared as the motive of the very first cults and therefore, the staple food of believers. In religious contexts, immortality often refers to the indefinite continuation of the soul or mind beyond physical death, a belief that has been a major point of focus and a source of comfort for many believers. However, immortality has acquired the dignity of a scientific subject, studied in laboratories attempting to understand the mechanisms of aging, hoping to control or neutralize them. It is now commonplace in the media to see explanations of the role of telomerase, the enzyme involved in the division of germ cells, to which the body turns for renewal. The opinion according to which senescence is a pathology that might soon be cured is increasingly pervasive—death is a simple disease that will be overcome with antioxidants and a careful diet. There is nothing natural about death, we hear, ever more frequently. *senescence: 노쇠","Medical practice was revolutionized by Hippocrates, the “father of Western medicine.” (A) He changed medicine in many ways. (B) For example, he was an advocate for publishing medical knowledge, focusing on patient care rather than diagnosis, and demanding that physicians act professionally. (C) That is, diet and living habits are linked to disease, and making modifications to them may help to reduce the occurrence or severity of certain diseases. (D) Hippocrates’ insights into the connections between environment, lifestyle, and health have had a lasting influence, laying the foundation for preventive medicine.","About a century ago, when General Motors had first proposed adding lead to petrol—in order to improve performance—scientists were alarmed. They urged the government to investigate the public health implications. Thomas Midgley, Jr., American engineer and chemist who discovered the effectiveness of tetraethyl lead as an antiknock additive for gasoline, breezily assured government officials that “the average street will probably be so free from lead that it will be impossible to detect it or its absorption,” although he conceded that “no actual experimental data has been taken.” General Motors funded a government bureau to conduct some research, adding a clause saying it had to approve the findings. (3 pts.)","Toxicology is the science of adverse effects of chemical substances on living organisms. Living organisms include the algae in the sea, animals and people, all flora and fauna. There are no safe substances, all chemicals can be poisonous and cause injury or death. But they can be used safely: the effect depends on the dose and exposure. It is possible by limiting these to handle and benefit from the properties of chemical substances in an ‘acceptably safe’ way. Toxicological studies aim to assess the adverse effects related to different doses in order to find this ‘acceptably safe’ level.","Artificial Intelligence (AI) is revolutionizing the way we live and work, with applications in various fields such as healthcare, education, and transportation. AI systems can learn, solve problems, and plan, imitating human intelligence and senses like visual perception and speech recognition. However, AI also presents challenges, such as the need to evaluate and recognize truth in the information it generates. As AI continues to evolve, it is crucial for individuals to develop critical thinking skills and learn how to verify the accuracy of information presented by AI systems. This will ensure that the benefits of AI are maximized while potential risks are minimized.","Intellectual property rights (IPR) have been defined as ideas, inventions, and creative expressions based on which there is a public willingness to bestow the status of property. IPR provide certain exclusive rights to the inventors or creators of that property, in order to enable them to reap commercial benefits from their creative efforts or reputation. There are several types of intellectual property protection like patent, copyright, trademark, etc. IPR is prerequisite for better identification, planning, commercialization, rendering, and thereby protection of invention or creativity. Each industry should evolve its own IPR policies, management style, strategies, and so on depending on its area of specialty. Pharmaceutical industry currently has an evolving IPR strategy requiring a better focus and approach in the coming era.","“From the time you’re a baby to the time you die, you’re an individual who wants to be recognized and respected,” Hirami said. She says children start to understand this through their daily interactions with multiple age groups. This understanding shapes their social development and sense of self-worth throughout their lives. (2 pts.)","While opinions differ wildly about what the ramifications for society will be if the human lifespan is extended, most ethicists agree that the issue should be discussed now, since it might be impossible to stop or control the technology once it’s developed. “If this could ever happen, then we’d better ask what kind of society we want to get,” Mike Callahan, an ethicist at Harvard University said, “We had better not go anywhere near it until we have figured those problems out.”","Newspaper articles __________________: some element of lying is inherent in all journalism because it is impossible for one article to include all the details of the story. Journalists may also manipulate the order in which they present information to achieve more drama or other effects in their writing. Choosing details and the order to describe them is considered proper and ethical behavior for journalists. Editors can even reflect their paper’s political bias when writing opinion pieces about elections and politics.","Scott’s expedition brought back 40,000 scientific items, including almost 20 kilograms of rock. Of the 2,000 animal and plant species the expedition brought back, some 400 were new discoveries. The most important fossil, located next to Scott’s body, was a tree from 250 million years ago. running low on food, the explorers went in a different direction to enable them to find this fossil. The tree had only been found in Australia, Africa, and South America. So finding it in the Antarctic was proof that these countries and continents had all been joined together in the past.","(A) Moor has the essayist’s gift for making new connections, the adventurer’s love for paths untaken, and the philosopher’s knack for asking big questions. With a breathtaking arc that spans from the dawn of animal life to the digital era, On Trails is a book that makes us see our world, our history, our species, and our ways of life anew. (B) While thru-hiking the Appalachian Trail, Moor began to wonder about the paths that lie beneath our feet: How do they form? Why do some improve over time while others fade? What makes us follow or strike off on our own? Over the course of seven years, Moor traveled the globe, exploring trails of all kinds, from the miniscule to the massive. He learned the tricks of master trail-builders, hunted down long-lost Cherokee trails, and traced the origins of our road networks and the Internet. In each chapter, Moor interweaves his adventures with findings from science, history, philosophy, and nature writing. (C) Throughout, Moor reveals how this single topic— the oft-overlooked trail—sheds new light on a wealth of age-old questions: How does order emerge out of chaos? How did animals first crawl forth from the seas and spread across continents? How has humanity’s relationship with nature and technology shaped world around us? And, ultimately, how does each of us pick a path through life?"],"questions":[{"q":1,"stem":"The illustration had too much redundant detail. The artist should consider streamlining it to enhance its clarity and impact.","opts":["deficient","superfluous","inadequate","incompetent"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":0,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"redundant는 ‘중복되는, 과다한’이란 의미이다. 그래서 예술가는 명확성과 효과를 높이기 위해 그 삽화를 정리해야 한다고 덧붙인다. 보기 중에서 ‘과잉의, 여분의’의 뜻을 갖는 것은 ②superfluous이다."},{"q":2,"stem":"Any attack by enemy soldiers will hamper the arrival of food rations for our troops.","opts":["hinder","assist","facilitate","decelerate"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":0,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"hamper는 ‘방해하다, 훼방하다’라는 의미이다. ‘적군의 공격은 우리 군대에 대한 식 량 공급의 도착을 방해할 것’이라는 내용의 문장이다. 보기 중에서 ‘방해하다’는 의미의 단어는 ①hinder이다. assist는 ‘돕다,’ facilitate는 ‘촉진하다,’ decelerate는 ‘속도를 줄이다’는 의미이다."},{"q":3,"stem":"What others say and do is a projection of their reality and perception, not yours.","opts":["scheme","operation","proposal","manifestation"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":0,"psg":null,"a":4,"ex":"‘다른 사람들이 이야기하고 행하는 것은 그들의 현실과 관념에 대한 투영이지 당신의 것이 아니다’라는 의미이므로, ‘투영(projection)’과 의미상 가장 가까운 단어는 ④ manifestation(표현, 표시)이다."},{"q":4,"stem":"Today's business environment makes it impossible for organizations to afford to squander any resources.","opts":["dissipate","engender","assemble","accumulate"],"pts":3.0,"inline":false,"sec":0,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"squander는 ‘낭비하다, 탕진하다’의 의미이다. dissipate는 ‘낭비하다, 다 써버리다’ 이고, engender는 ‘발생시키다,’ assemble은 ‘모으다,’ accumulate는 ‘축적하다’의 의미이므로 squander와 의미가 유사한 단어는 ①dissipate이다."},{"q":5,"stem":"North Americans often hold off a certain distance in conversation, which is about 21 inches apart found by studies.","opts":["cease","initiate","withdraw","maintain"],"pts":2.0,"inline":false,"sec":0,"psg":null,"a":4,"ex":"hold off는 ‘(거리, 간격)을 유지하다’는 의미이므로 보기 중에서는 ④maintain이 가 장 의미가 유사하다. cease는 ‘그만 두다,’ initiate는 ‘시작하다,’ withdraw는 ‘철수하다, 회수하다’ 등의 의미로 뒤에 목적어 distance를 갖기에 어색한 표현들이다."},{"q":6,"stem":"It's important for writers to avoid using excessive __________ in their work, as it can alienate readers who are not familiar with specialized terms.","opts":["slang","jargon","parley","altercation"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":1,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"괄호 안에 들어간 명사를 ‘과도하게 쓰면, 전문적인 용어들에 익숙하지 않은 독자들을 소외시킬 수 있다’는 내용의 문장이다. 따라서 빈칸에는 ‘전문 용어’를 뜻하는 ② jargon이 들어가는 것이 가장 적합하다. slang은 ‘속어’, altercation은 ‘언쟁,’ parley 는 ‘회담, 교섭’이란 의미이다."},{"q":7,"stem":"In the midst of the intense pain, Maximilian's efforts to form coherent words were in vain; his unsteady movements led him to lean against the wall, fighting to remain upright. Maximilian tried to speak, but he could _____________ nothing; he staggered, and supported himself against the wall.","opts":["refer","verify","describe","articulate"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":1,"psg":null,"a":4,"ex":"‘격심한 고통 때문에 맥시밀리언이 분명한 말들로 표현할 수 없었다’는 내용이므로 빈칸에는 ‘분명하게 말하다’는 의미의 ④articulate가 들어가는 것이 적합하다."},{"q":8,"stem":"In a last-ditch effort, the suspect chose to _____________ for mercy, hoping to avoid the maximum penalty.","opts":["plead","require","demand","litigate"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":1,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"‘plead for mercy’는 ‘자비를 베풀어달라고 간청하다’는 의미이다. require, demand 는 ‘요구하다’는 의미이지만 타동사로 뒤에 전치사 없이 목적어가 바로 와야 하며, litigate 역시 타동사로 ‘소송하다’는 의미이다."},{"q":9,"stem":"An engineer wears a helmet of sensors—part of a brain scanner that requires _______________.","opts":["as almost much power as a nuclear submarine","almost as much power as a nuclear submarine","as much almost as power as a nuclear submarine","as much as power as an almost nuclear submarine"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"‘엔지니어가 쓰고 있는 감지장치헬멧은 거의 핵잠수함수준의 전력을 요구하는 뇌스 캔장치’라는 내용이므로 가장 적절한 어순은 ②almost as much power as a nuclear submarine이라야 한다."},{"q":10,"stem":"I used to hold two assumptions: one, poor people are poor in part because they’re uneducated and don’t make good choices; two, they then need people like me to figure out what they need and get it to them. It turns out, the evidence says __________. Dozens of studies indicate that people use direct financial assistance to enhance their own lives in various ways, such as food, security, housing, healthcare, and education.","opts":["besides","otherwise","likewise","in the end"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"자신이 가지고 있었던 두 가지 전제(가난한 사람들은 교육받지 못했고 스스로 선택할 능력이 없다/누군가가 그들을 대신해 더 나은 선택을 해주어야 한다)를 뒤집는 연 구 결과에 관한 내용이다. 빈칸 다음에는 이러한 생각을 뒤집는 결과를 설명하므로 답은 ②otherwise이다."},{"q":11,"stem":"In 1989, 170 nations signed the Basel Convention to address the problem of the international trade in waste. The agreement required developed nations to notify developing nations of hazardous waste shipments coming into the country. Six years later, after pressure from environmental groups and developing nations, the Basel Convention ____________________ hazardous waste shipments to poor countries completely.","opts":["modified banning","was modified to ban","was to modify banning","was modified to be banned"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"‘가난한 나라로 위험한 쓰레기를 실어 보내는 것을 완전히 금지하도록’ 바젤 협약이 개정되었다고 해야 올바른 내용이 된다. 문법적으로는 to 부정사를 목적보어로 하는 5형식의 수동태를 만드는 문장이다. ‘주어+동사+목적어+to 부정사’가 수동태로 바뀌 어서 ‘주어+be동사+p.p.+to 부정사’가 되는 구문이다. 즉, ‘People modified the Basel Convention to ban hazardous shipments...’를 수동태로 바꾸어서 ‘the Basel Convention was modified to ban hazardous shipments...’가 된다."},{"q":12,"stem":"_______________ without loads of salt and butter, popcorn can be an excellent healthy snack that contains a surprising amount of nutrients.","opts":["Preparing","To prepare","When prepared","Unless you prepare"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"‘소금과 버터를 뿌리지 않고 준비된다면 팝콘은 훌륭한 건강 간식이 될 수 있다’는 내용이다. 문장 전체의 주어가 popcorn이므로 분사구문의 수동형이 되어야 한다 (When (it is) prepared...). 그런데 When 이하의 주어 it이 주절의 주어 popcorn과 같으므로 주어와 be동사가 함께 생략되어 When prepared만 남는다."},{"q":13,"stem":"Predictive genetic testing poses ethical and practical dilemmas. Personally, I don’t think knowing whether I have the potential to develop an incurable disease will, in any way, enhance the quality of my life, _______________ interpret the genetic test results without the help of a medical professional.","opts":["I nor would be able to","nor would I be able to","nor I would be able to","I would nor be able to"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"빈칸 앞에 I don’t think로 시작하는 부정문이 왔다. 그 내용은 ‘불치병 잠재 요소가 있다는 것을 아는게 내 삶의 질을 증진시킨다고 생각하지 않는다’이다. 쉼표 뒤에도 ‘의학 전문가의 도움 없이는 유전자 검사 결과를 해석할 수 없을 것’이라는 부정문이 이어진다. 이 부정문을 이끄는 접속사는 nor인데 하나의 절이 부정 접속어 nor로 시 작하면 그 뒤는 주어와 동사가 도치된다. 따라서 ②nor would I be able to가 정답이다."},{"q":14,"stem":"Some British scientists suggest _______________ a bottom-up method. This contrasts with their view of top-down approaches in the study of animal behavior.","opts":["that they term","which is termed","what they term","where they term"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"문장의 의미로 보아 ‘영국의 과학자들이 a bottom-up method라고 부르는 것’이라는 내용이 들어가야 한다. 따라서 선행사를 포함하는 관계대명사 what이 이끄는 ③ what they term이 가장 적절하다."},{"q":15,"stem":"A few bones of Spinosaurus have been found in the deserts of Egypt and were described about 100 years ago by a German paleontologist. Unfortunately, ①all his Spinosaurus bones were destroyed in World War II. So all ②we’re left with are just a few drawings and notes. From these drawings, we can see this creature, which lived about 100 million years ago, was very big and it had tall spines ③on its back, forming a magnificent sail, and it had long, slender jaws like a crocodile with conical teeth that ④may have used to catch slippery prey like fish.","opts":["all his","we’re left","on its","may have"],"pts":2.5,"inline":true,"sec":3,"psg":null,"a":4,"ex":"공룡의 모습을 복원하는 내용이다. 마지막 문장에서 conical teeth that ④may have used to catch slippery prey like fish는 ‘물고기 같은 미끄러운 먹이를 잡을 때 사용된 원뿔형 이빨’이라는 의미이므로 수동형 may have been used to라고 바꾸어야 한다."},{"q":16,"stem":"I once worked with this woman who after 20 years of marriage and an extremely ugly divorce, was finally ready for her first date. Ten minutes into the date, the man stands up and says, “I’m not interested,” and walks out. The woman was so hurt she couldn’t move. All she could do ①was call a friend. Here’s what the friend said: “Well, what do you expect? You have big hips, you have nothing interesting to say, ②why would a handsome, successful man like that ever go out with a loser like you?” Shocking, right, that a friend could be so cruel? But it would be much less shocking if I told you it wasn’t the friend who said that. It’s what the woman said to herself. We all start thinking of all our faults and all our shortcomings ③maybe not as harshly, but ④we all doing it.","opts":["was call","why would","maybe not","we all"],"pts":3.0,"inline":true,"sec":3,"psg":null,"a":4,"ex":"①은 ‘친구에게 전화하는 것’이라는 명사적 보어가 와야 하는데, ‘to call’을 쓰기보 다는 ‘to’를 생략한 원형부정사 ‘call’을 쓰는 것이 일반적인 표현이다. ②는 상상 속에서 스스로에게 질문하는 내용이므로 ‘why would ... a man ... go out?’이라는 직접 의문문이 올바른 형태이다. ③은 ‘어쩌면 (이만큼) 가혹하지는 않게’를 뜻하는 구문이 들어가야 하므로 ‘as that’이 생략된 올바른 표현이다. ④는 ‘주어+동사’를 이 끄는 절 두 개를 등위접속사 but이 연결하고 있는 구문이므로, but 뒤에 주어와 동사가 와야 한다. 따라서 ④는 ‘we all do it’이 되어야 옳다."},{"q":17,"stem":"Apple first became the world’s most valuable stock in 2011, when its market cap was under $340 billion and it comprised about 3.3% of the S&P 500. Since then, it has rarely __________ that title. It first reached $1 trillion in value in mid-2018, and it achieved a $2 trillion valuation in August 2020, making it the first US company to surpass that level.","opts":["held","forfeited","waived","involved"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"‘애플 주식이 2011년 가장 가치 있는 주식으로 등극한 이후 그 자리를 놓친 적이 거의 없다’는 내용이므로 빈칸에는 ②forfeited(상실했다)가 가장 적절하다. ③의 waive는 ‘철회하다’는 뜻이다."},{"q":18,"stem":"In this book, “everyday heroes” are not those that personify physical bravery. Though heroes such as firefighters are by no means less praiseworthy, I chose to feature passionate promoters of social justice and equality. Their work is humanitarian in nature. They are founders or leaders of successful nonprofits, representing a diverse range of _______________ and people. Nearly all self-identify as social entrepreneurs.","opts":["causes","cultures","sectors","corporates"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"이 글에서는 ‘매일의 영웅들’에 대해 이야기한다. 그런데 그 영웅들은 신체적인 용감 함보다는 오히려 ‘사회적 정의나 평등을 열정적으로 증진하는 사람들(passionate promoters of social justice and equality)’이고 ‘그들이 하는 일이 본질적으로 인도 주의적이며(Their work is humanitarian in nature),’ 스스로를 ‘사회적 기업가’라고 생각한다. 빈칸에는 그들이 대표하는 다양한(representing a diverse range of ...) 대 상이 들어가야 하는데 ‘사회적 정의나 평등’ ‘인도주의적 일’ 등을 보면 ‘주의, 주장, 대의, 명분’을 뜻하는 ①causes가 적합하다."},{"q":19,"stem":"Many people fear failure and try to avoid it even when they have the opportunity to succeed. As a result, many people won’t attempt something if they think they might fail. __________ their view so that failure is fine and nothing to worry about could be the key to opening new opportunities to be successful in life.","opts":["Altering","Ignoring","Collecting","Confirming"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"‘많은 사람들은 실패를 두려워해서 시도조차 않기 때문에 성공할 기회를 놓친다’는 내용의 글이다. 빈칸 다음에는 실패도 괜찮고 걱정할 것이 없다는 방식으로 견해를 ‘바꾸는 것’이 되어야 내용이 자연스러우므로 ①Altering이 들어가야 적절하다."},{"q":20,"stem":"As K-pop continues its global ascendancy, it is expected to become even more diverse, with an increasing number of independent artists breaking into the scene. Despite the industry’s rigid standards, K-pop artists are ___________________ norms through sophisticated subtexts and modern themes.","opts":["finding ways challenging","to find ways challenging","finding ways to challenge","to find ways to be challenging"],"pts":2.0,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"K-pop의 전지구적인 인기에 관해 설명하면서, ‘업계의 엄격한 기준에도 불구하고 K-pop 아티스트들은 정교한 함의와 현대적인 주제를 통해 규범에 도전한다’는 내용의 글이다. 빈칸에 들어갈 내용은 ‘규범을 도전하는 방식을 찾아나가는 중’이라는 표 현이므로 ③finding ways to challenge가 적절하다."},{"q":21,"stem":"Most people around the world are right-handed. This fact also seems to have held true throughout history. According to studies, two right-handed parents have only a 9.5 percent chance of having a left-handed child, (A) two left-handed parents have a 26 percent chance. One simple idea suggests that people normally get right-handedness from their parents, and another common theory is that left-handed people suffer mild brain damage during birth. (B) , if this theory were true, it would not explain why the percentage of left-handed people is so similar in every society. Whatever the reasons behind it, people’s attitudes toward left-handedness changed a lot over the years.","opts":["(A) whereas (B) However","(A) yet (B) In addition","(A) all the while (B) Therefore","(A) because (B) On the other hand"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"빈칸 (A)앞에는 ‘부모가 모두 오른손잡이일 경우 왼손잡이 자녀 출생 비율,’ 빈칸 뒤 에서는 ‘부모가 모두 왼손잡이일 경우 왼손잡이 자녀의 출생비율’을 대조하고 있으므로 ‘...한 반면에’라는 의미의 whereas가 가장 적합하다. 빈칸 (B)는 그 앞에서 제시한 ‘왼손잡이 가설’--출생시 가벼운 뇌손상이 원인--을 반박하는 내용을 시작하는 부분이므로 역접을 나타내는 접속부사 However가 적절하다."},{"q":22,"stem":"Frequently, engineering students arrive at university armed with good qualifications. However, they are vague about the kind and quality of impact they can make on society when they leave three to four years later. One of the ways in which engineering education programs demonstrate _______________ to society is in addressing pressing concerns, such as poverty alleviation and sustainable development in emerging nations.","opts":["relevance","complexity","exclusivity","profitability"],"pts":3.0,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"이 글의 앞부분은 공학 전공 대학생들이 사회에 미칠 수 있는 영향력의 종류와 특성에 대해 모호해한다는 내용이다. 빈칸이 들어간 문장에서는 이런 학생들이 사회와의 ‘관련성’을 보여줄 수 있는 방법에 관해 이야기하고 있다. 따라서 빈칸에는 ‘관련성’ 을 뜻하는 ①relevance가 적합하다."},{"q":23,"stem":"Just what is a role model? First, let’s recognize _______________. It is not necessarily the smartest, strongest, or most successful person you know— although it could be. A role model is a person who has the characteristics you want for yourself and who can help you develop those traits.","opts":["what it is","what he is","what it is not","what he is not"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"이 글은 롤모델에 관해 이야기한다. 롤모델이 무엇인가라는 질문을 던진 뒤, 먼저 ‘롤모델이란 무엇이 아닌지’를 알아보자고 한다. 빈칸 다음의 문장에서는 롤모델이란 반드시 이러저러할 필요는 없다고 이야기하고 있기 때문이다. 따라서 빈칸에는 ‘그것 (롤모델)이 아닌 것’을 뜻하는 ③what it is not이 적합하다. 롤모델은 사람일 수 있지만 이 글에서는 시종일관 it이란 대명사로 받고 있다는 점에 유의해야 한다."},{"q":24,"stem":"Leo is immeasurably wise. He has so much knowledge and experience and is interested in so many _______________ subjects, like Greek history, diamond mining, dinosaurs, and alternative medicine. Even though they are not related he enjoys them all.","opts":["diverse","academic","technical","specialized"],"pts":2.0,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"빈칸 다음에 오는 like는 앞에 오는 명사의 예를 보여준다. 그리스 역사, 다이아몬드 광업, 공룡, 대체 의학 등의 예는 서로간 관련이 없고(they are not related) ‘다양한’ 주제들이라고 할 수 있다. 따라서 ‘다양한’을 뜻하는 ①diverse가 적합하다."},{"q":25,"stem":"Modern Paris sits above limestone and gypsum. Over 2,000 years ago, the Romans were the first to mine these stones, leaving behind large holes in the ground and tunnels where the stones had been removed. In the beginning, these tunnels lay beyond the city limits, but as Paris grew, ___________________. In December 1774, a tunnel collapsed, swallowing houses and people.","opts":["it dug deeper into them","it was built around them","it spread out above them","more land was reclaimed"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"로마인들이 땅속의 석회석과 석고를 채굴해 간 후, 빈 공간이 터널들로 남았는데, 파리시가 커지면서 그러한 터널들 위로 확장되어서, 도시의 무게를 견디지 못한 터널들이 붕괴되었다는 내용이다. 그러므로 파리시가 터널들 위로 뻗어나갔다는 뜻이 되는 ③it spread out above them이 정답이다."},{"q":26,"stem":"Which is the best title of the passage?","opts":["The Impact of Diet on Aging and Lifespan","The Evolution of Immortality: From Religion to Science","The Path to Immortality: Antioxidants and Careful Diets","The Illusion of Death: How Science is Overcoming Aging"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":0,"a":2,"ex":"불멸(Immortality)이 더 이상 종교적 영역이 아니라 과학으로 넘어오게 되었음을 고 찰하는 글이다. 이 글의 앞부분에서는 종교적 견지에서 보는 불멸에 관해 설명하고, 뒷부분에서는 과학의 관점에서 노화는 ‘산화방지제와 주의 깊은 식단으로 극복될 수 있는 질병(a simple disease that will be overcome with antioxidants and a careful diet)’으로 보게 되었다고 묘사하므로 이 글에 적합한 제목으로는 ②불멸의 진화: 종교에서 과학으로(The Evolution of Immortality: From Religion to Science) 이다."},{"q":27,"stem":"Choose the most suitable position of the sentence below in the above passage. He also recognized that some diseases could be caused by the environment.","opts":["(A)","(B)","(C)","(D)"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":1,"a":3,"ex":"박스 안에 들어가 있는 문장은 ‘그는 또한 어떤 질병이 환경에 의해 발생할 수도 있 다는 것을 인식했다’는 의미이다. (C) 다음에 오는 문장을 보면 환경에 속하는 ‘식사 법과 생활 습관이 질병과 연관되어 있다’는 이야기로 환경으로 인한 질병에 관해 더 상세하게 설명하고 있다. 따라서 박스의 문장이 들어가기에는 (C)가 적합하다."},{"q":28,"stem":"Which is implied in the passage about General Motors?","opts":["It was unaware of the potential dangers of lead in petrol.","It actively suppressed evidence regarding the toxicity of lead in petrol.","It conducted thorough and unbiased research on the effects of lead in petrol.","It added a condition to research funding to approve findings before publication."],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":2,"a":4,"ex":"자동차회사 General Motors가 엔진 효율을 위해 휘발유에 납을 첨가하게 된 사건을 설명하는 글이다. 학계의 반대가 있었음에도 불구하고 General Motors 쪽에서는 자 신들의 발견을 승인해주는 쪽으로 연구 결과를 은밀히 조종한 배경이 마지막 문장에 드러나 있다."},{"q":29,"stem":"Which is NOT suggested in the above passage?","opts":["All chemicals can potentially cause poisoning and harm at certain doses.","The effect of a chemical substance depends on the dose and exposure.","Toxicological studies aim to find an ‘acceptably safe’ level of chemical exposure.","Toxicology is the study of the beneficial effects of chemical substances on living organisms."],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":3,"a":4,"ex":"독물학(Toxicology)은 ‘유기체에 대한 화학 물질의 해로운 영향을 연구하는 학문 (science of adverse effects of chemical substances on living organisms)’이라는 정의에 따라, ④‘독물학은 생명체에 대한 화학 물질의 유익한 영향을 연구하는 학문’ 이라는 선택지는 본문의 내용과 반대된다."},{"q":30,"stem":"According to the passage, what should we do to utilize AI effectively?","opts":["We should only use AI for simple, repetitive tasks and not for complex problem-solving.","We should avoid using AI until it is perfected and can operate without any human oversight.","We should replace human decision-making with AI to ensure maximum efficiency in all sectors.","We should cultivate our ability to think critically and learn how to authenticate the information that AI systems provide."],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":4,"a":4,"ex":"이 글은 앞부분에서 AI의 발전과 활용에 관해 이야기하고 However 이하에서는 이같이 AI가 진화하는 시대에 우리가 해야 할 일에 관해 이야기한다. ‘개인들은 비판적 사고 기술을 개발하고 AI 시스템이 제시하는 정보의 정확성을 입증할 방법을 배워야한다’고 말하고 있으므로 우리가 AI를 효율적으로 사용하기 위해서 해야 할 일로는 ‘비판적으로 생각하는 능력을 개발하고 AI 시스템이 제공하는 정보의 진위를 확인하는 법을 배워야 한다.’는 내용의 ④가 적절하다."},{"q":31,"stem":"What is the main purpose of IPR in the pharmaceutical industry?","opts":["To restrict access to new drugs and treatments","To promote sharing of all pharmaceutical innovations","To limit the types of intellectual property protection available","To enable inventors and creators to benefit commercially from their innovations"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":5,"a":4,"ex":"지적재산권(IPR)의 정의(창작물에 대한 재산권수여)--목적(창작물에 대한 상업적 이 윤 보장)--종류(특허, 저작권, 상표)--제약업계의 사례로 이어지는 글이다. 질문은 제약업계에서의 지적재산권 사용 목적을 묻고 있는데 글의 중반부 지적재산권의 목적에 대한 설명 부분을 보면 in order to enable them to reap commercial benefits from their creative efforts or reputation이라는 내용이 명시되어 있다."},{"q":32,"stem":"Which best explains the main idea of the above passage?","opts":["A friend is known in necessity.","Respect is a basic human need.","Empty vessels make the most sound.","Heaven helps those who help themselves."],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":6,"a":2,"ex":"‘모든 연령대의 사람들이 다 귀하다’는 가르침을 아이들이 다양한 연령대의 사람들 과의 접촉을 통해서 배운다는 이야기이므로, 해당 글의 주제로는 ②‘존중은 인간의 기본적인 욕구이다’가 적합하다."},{"q":33,"stem":"Which is implied in the passage?","opts":["The human lifespan will definitely be extended in the near future.","The technology to extend the human lifespan is already developed and ready for use.","Most ethicists believe that the issue of extended human lifespan should be discussed now to avoid potential societal issues.","Mike Callahan believes that the technology to extend the human lifespan should be developed without considering the consequences."],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":7,"a":3,"ex":"이 글은 수명 연장이 사회에 미치는 의미에 관해서는 의견이 다양할 수 있지만, 일 단 그 기술이 개발되고 나면 멈추거나 통제하는 것이 불가능할 수 있으므로 그 문제에 대해 지금 논의가 이루어져야 한다는 윤리학자들의 주장을 소개한다. Mike Callahan이 주장하는 내용도 같다. 따라서 이 글에서 암시하는 것은 ‘많은 윤리학자 들은 잠재적인 사회 문제를 피할 수 있도록 인간의 수명 연장 주제는 지금 논의되어 야 한다고 믿는다는 것이다.’ 따라서 ③이 정답이다."},{"q":34,"stem":"Which is true to the above passage?","opts":["Newspaper articles are always unable to convey the complete truth.","All journalists are required to include every detail of a story in their articles.","Journalists are not allowed to manipulate the order of information in their writing.","Editors are prohibited from reflecting their paper’s political bias in opinion pieces."],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":8,"a":1,"ex":"이 글에서 이야기하는 것은 신문 기사는 그 기사를 쓰는 사람이 어떤 사건의 모든 세부 사항들을 다 포함할 수도 없고, 또 특정한 효과를 내기 위해 순서도 바꾸고 하 기 때문에 ‘신문 기사란 항상 완벽한 진실을 전달할 수 없다’는 것이다. 따라서 이 글의 내용과 맞는 것은 ①이다."},{"q":35,"stem":"Which is the most suitable for the blank?","opts":["should try to be equitable","should be read with scrutiny","can never tell the entire truth","can sometimes make ficticious stories"],"pts":2.0,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":8,"a":3,"ex":"이 글 전체에서 이야기하는 내용은 ‘신문 기사란 모든 세부사항을 포함할 수 없고, 또 발생 순서를 바꾸는 등으로 인해 완전한 진실을 말할 수 없다’는 것이다. 이 글을 여는 첫 문장에서도 이와 관련된 내용이 들어가야 한다. 따라서 ③(신문 기사는) ‘결 코 전체적 진실을 말할 수 없다’가 적합하다."},{"q":36,"stem":"Which is the most emphasized in the above passage?","opts":["The role of teamwork in survival situations","The physical hardships endured by Scott's team","The importance of scientific discovery in Scott's expedition","The significance of the tree fossil in proving continental drift"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":9,"a":3,"ex":"이 글은 스콧의 탐험대가 남극에서 매우 활발한 과학적 탐사 활동을 벌였다는 이야 기를 담고 있다. 식량도 부족하고 아마도 추위와 싸우며 극점을 향해 가느라 분투하 면서도 중요한 과학적 발견을 놓치지 않으려던 탐험대의 노력을 강조하는 글이므로, ③이 정답이다. ①, ②번은 거의 언급되지 않았고, ④는 스콧 탐험대가 이룬 공헌의 예로 든 것이다."},{"q":37,"stem":"Which is the most suitable for the blank?","opts":["Under","Despite","At the cost of","Instead of"],"pts":3.0,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":9,"a":2,"ex":"‘식량이 다 떨어져감’에도 불구하고 탐사를 포기하지 않았다는 내용이 되어야 하므로, ②despite가 정답이다."},{"q":38,"stem":"Choose the appropriate order of the paragraphs.","opts":["(A) - (C) - (B)","(B) - (A) - (C)","(B) - (C) - (A)","(C) - (A) - (B)"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":10,"a":3,"ex":"무어가 쓴 책 On Trails에 대한 리뷰이다. (B)책을 쓰게 된 계기와 과정--(C)책 전 체에 걸쳐 트레일이라는 단일 토픽이 자연-기술-인생과 철학으로 뻗어나가는 과정 --(A)완성된 책에 대한 최종적 평으로 연결되어야 가장 자연스럽다."},{"q":39,"stem":"What did Moor explore during his seven-year journey?","opts":["The history of the Appalachian Trail","The techniques of master trail-builders","The origins of the Internet and road networks","The formation and evolution of trails and paths"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":10,"a":4,"ex":"(B)단락의 중반에서 작가는 7년간 지구촌을 탐사하고 과학적, 역사적, 철학적, 자연 관찰적 글쓰기를 섭렵하며 책에 녹여 넣었다고 했으므로 선택지 중 가장 포괄적인 내 용인 ④The formation and evolution of trails and paths가 답이 되어야 한다."},{"q":40,"stem":"Which is the best title of the passage?","opts":["Trails: An Exploration of Paths and Life","The Philosophy of Trails: A Global Exploration","The Evolution of Trails: From Ant Paths to the Internet","The Wisdom of Trails: A Journey Through Time and Space"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":10,"a":1,"ex":"‘On Trails라는 책에서 다루는 길과 인생의 전반적인 의미’를 리뷰하고 평가하는 글이므로 답은 ①Trails: An Exploration of Paths and Life가 가장 자연스럽다."}]},"2025":{"sections":["Choose the one that is closest in meaning to the underlined word(s).","Choose the one that best fills in the blank.","Choose the one that most grammatically completes the sentence.","Choose the one that is grammatically INCORRECT.","Choose the one(s) that best complete(s) the sentence.","Read the following passages and answer the questions."],"passages":["Moreland and Beach asked one female research assistant to attend a college class fifteen times during the semester, a second research assistant to attend ten times, a third to attend five times, and a fourth research assistant not to attend at all. Then, at the end of the semester, all four of them came to the classroom, and the researchers asked all students in the class to rate how much they liked each of the four women. The assistants were fairly similar in appearance, and none interacted with any of the students during the semester.","I climbed the ladder, heard my dive announced, and began the steps and jumps that would throw me into the air. (A) Pushing off the diving board with my legs, I lifted my arms and shoulders back. (B) I knew immediately that I was going to be close to the board and that I might hit my hands. (C) Then I heard a strange sound and felt my body lose control. (D) Moments later I realized what had happened; I had hit my head on the diving board.","Physiologist Ancel Keys was both the world's best known champion of the Mediterranean diet and its best advertisement. Keys was the first to notice, more than half a century ago, that heart disease was rare in Mediterranean areas like Greece and southern Italy, where olive oil and red wine were dietary staples and people ate plenty of fruits and vegetables. Keys died at the age of 100, still active and doing nutrition research until the last few years of his life. In an interview with WebMD in 2000, he lamented the fact that the typical meat, cheese, and pasta-heavy dishes Americans encounter in Italian restaurants have little in common with traditional Mediterranean fare. \"The Mediterranean diet was nearly vegetarian, with fish and very little meat, and was rich in green vegetables,\" he said adding that something got lost in the translation from Italy to the U.S. \"They may call it Italian, but it's very different from the food we studied.“","Thailand is not the birthplace of the Capsicum, or chili pepper; it only acts as if it is. In fact, the chili was imported, along with much else in the national diet. However, in Thailand the per capita consumption of the small, fiery fruit is surely as high if not higher than it is anywhere else. And it is in the use of unprocessed, fresh, ripe chilis where Thailand rings all the loudest bells.","In 2002, the U.S. exported waste and scrap to China with an estimated value of $1.2 billion, up from $194 million five years earlier, according to Commerce Department data. Scrap is now the nation's third largest export to China, after airplanes and semiconductors and ahead of soybeans and computers. \"We are the Saudi Arabia of scrap,\" says Robert Garino, director of commodity research at the Washington-based Institute of Scrap Recycling Industries. China has become the biggest customer for America's junk, buying 23% of the $5.2 billion in scrap and waste exports.","Stream of consciousness is a literary technique that arose around the mid to late 19th century. The term itself is usually attributed to the British writer May Sinclair. The method allows authors to depict a character's perception randomly and spontaneously. Structure and form matter little. The purpose of stream of consciousness is to capture the whole experience of a character at a given moment. Many authors believe this is the closest they can get to the essence of their characters. A written record of individual internal thoughts and feelings in the rawest form defines this style. Notable writers such as James Joyce and William Faulkner employed this technique.","Many people use both mainstream treatments and CAM, or Complementary and Alternative Medicine, to get \"the best of both worlds.\" Conventional medicine, sometimes nicknamed \"rescue medicine,\" is still the norm for acute injuries that require emergency medical attention. However, the holistic approach of CAM is often preferred for chronic conditions. Chronic pain, for example, could be treated with a mixture of yoga, acupuncture, meditation and natural remedies. Besides pain relief, patients also benefit from an overall improvement in health. Homeopathy is a good example of how CAM treats the whole patient. The principle of homeopathy is \"________.\" A homeopathic fever remedy would, for example, cause a fever in a healthy person. When given to a fever patient, however, it will trigger the sufferer's body to heal itself. This is why the patient normally feels worse before feeling better — it is the patient's own body, not the remedy, that is doing the healing.","You might never guess that the word sincere is related to making pottery. Some language experts say that sincere comes from two Latin words: sin meaning “without” and cero meaning “wax.” Thus, sincere means “without wax.” In ancient times, people used pottery made of clay for plates and bowls. It took a long time to make this pottery. Occasionally, the pottery had cracks in it and was not good quality. Some potters who did not want to make brand-new pottery put wax on the crack to (A) the mistake. To the eye of a careless shopper, the pottery looked good. However, people soon realized which potters were good and which were not. Thus, the most (B) potters made pottery that was without wax, or “sincere,” and that is how the word sincere came to mean honest or truthful in thoughts and actions.","Some insects use trick pheromones to imitate other species. In some cases, this protects them from becoming the next course in another insect's meal. An interesting example is the Large Blue butterfly. During its caterpillar stage, this unusual insect releases a pheromone similar to that of an ant. If ants find a Large Blue caterpillar in the forest, they carry it home. There, instead of eating it, they care for it. The ants do not suspect that anything is wrong, even when the caterpillar starts to eat their young! The caterpillar doesn't leave the nest until it has safely turned into a butterfly. Yet another insect-like creature uses trick pheromones to attract its next meal. The bolas spider, a species common in South America and Africa, releases a pheromone similar to that produced by a female moth. The spider then waits for a male moth to arrive. Instead of finding a female, the ____________ moth becomes a tasty meal for the spider.","(A) This is true in such countries as the United States, Britain, and Germany. But in other cultures, such as Japan's, the message depends more on situations and feelings than it does on words. For this reason, the goal of many TV commercials in Japan will be to show how good people feel in a party or some other social situation. The commercial will not say that a product is better than others. Instead, its goal will be to create a positive mood or feeling about the product. (B) Most advertising firms are now beginning to write completely new ads. In writing new ads, global advertisers must consider different styles of communication in different countries. In some cultures, the meaning of an advertisement is usually found in the exact words that are used to describe the product and to explain why it is better than the competition. (C) It is true that the problems of global advertising — problems of language and culture — have become larger than ever. For example, Braniff Airlines wanted to advertise its fine leather seats. But when its advertisement was translated from English to Spanish, it told people that they could fly naked! Another example of wrong translation is when Chevrolet tried to market the Chevy Nova in Latin America. In English, the word nova refers to a star. But in Spanish, it means \"doesn't go.\" Would you buy a car with this name?"],"questions":[{"q":1,"stem":"Insufficient understanding of diseases can have a catastrophic effect on society.","opts":["extensive","auspicious","devastating","prominent"],"pts":2.0,"inline":false,"sec":0,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"catastrophic은 ‘파국을 초래하는’이라는 뜻이므로 ‘대단히 파괴적인, 엄청난 손상을 가하는’의 의미인 ③devastating이 정답이다."},{"q":2,"stem":"The profuse tropical forests of the Amazon are inhabited by different kinds of animals.","opts":["wild","sterile","distant","abundant"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":0,"psg":null,"a":4,"ex":"profuse는 ‘많은, 풍부한’이라는 뜻이므로 ‘풍부한’의 의미를 지닌 ④abundant가 정 답이다."},{"q":3,"stem":"For twelve years, Horace Mann pleaded the state government to improve the schools.","opts":["lectured","resisted","implored","consulted"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":0,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"plead는 ‘간청하다’는 의미의 동사이다. 유사한 의미를 가진 ③implore가 정답이다."},{"q":4,"stem":"Culinary tourists happily pay thousands of dollars for the privilege of sweating over a hot stove and then tucking into their own creations.","opts":["eating","appraising","boasting","displaying"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":0,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"tucking into~는 ‘~을 먹다’라는 뜻이므로 동일한 의미를 가진 ①eating이 정답이다."},{"q":5,"stem":"With the continued resolution of conservationists and local officials, experts project that the manatee population will continue to grow.","opts":["obsession","determination","formation","concentration"],"pts":2.0,"inline":false,"sec":0,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"resolution은 ‘과단성, 결단력, 결심’이라는 뜻이므로 유사한 의미를 가진 ②determination이 정답이다."},{"q":6,"stem":"Over millions of years, the continents slowly drifted apart to create the current continental __________.","opts":["conversion","conciliation","configuration","confrontation"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":1,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"수백 년간 대륙이 서서히 떠돌다가 현재의 대륙 배치, 지형을 만들었다는 내용이므로 빈칸에는 ③configuration ‘배치’가 정답이다."},{"q":7,"stem":"The United Nations officially began in October of 1945 when most of the original participating countries had __________ its charter.","opts":["ratified","disregarded","abolished","encountered"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":1,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"UN의 회원국들이 유엔 헌장을 비준한 후에 유엔이 공식적으로 성립되었다는 내용이므로 ①ratified ‘비준하다’가 가장 적절하다."},{"q":8,"stem":"Although Pompei was covered in ash from the eruption in 79 BC, the city was discovered relatively __________ in 1748.","opts":["intact","intimate","integral","intangible"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":1,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"Pompei가 화산폭발로 인해 재로 뒤덮였지만, Pompei 도시 자체는 비교적 온전한 상태로 발굴되었다는 의미이므로 ‘(하나도 손상되지 않고) 온전한’을 의미하는 ①intact가 정답이다."},{"q":9,"stem":"There are some reports which indicate that living near a nuclear power plant __________ living near a chemical plant or an oil refinery.","opts":["is as danger as","has the same danger in","is similarly dangerous as","is no more dangerous than"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":4,"ex":"비교급 [more + 형용사 + than] 구문으로 ‘핵발전소 근처에 사는 것은 화학 발전소 나 정유공장 인근에 사는 것보다 더 위험한 것은 아니다 (비슷하게 위험하다)’라는 의미로 ④is no more dangerous than이 정답이다. 그러나 ‘as ~ as’ 사이에는 형용 사가 필요하므로 ①은 as dangerous as의 형태를 이루어야 하며, ②는 has the same danger as로 되어야 한다."},{"q":10,"stem":"__________ as a sacred crop in China, soybeans are one of the richest plant sources of protein.","opts":["If revering","Once revered","When they revere","After they have revered"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"‘한때 콩은 중국에서 신성한 작물로 숭배되었던’이라는 의미이므로 수동의 의미를 가진 ②Once revered가 정답이다. Once they (soybeans) are revered에서 주어와 동사(they are)가 생략된 구조이다."},{"q":11,"stem":"American women usually identify their best friend as someone __________.","opts":["they talk frequently","is talking frequently","who talks frequently with","with whom they talk frequently"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":4,"ex":"관계대명사의 격을 묻는 문제이다. ‘미국 여성들은 이야기를 자주 나누는 사람을 친한 친구로 여긴다’는 내용으로 talk은 with와 함께 쓰여서 ‘~와 이야기를 나눈다’는 의미가 되고 해당 형용사절은 선행사 someone과 목적격 관계이므로 정답은 ④with whom they talk frequently이다."},{"q":12,"stem":"Emily Dickinson penned over 1,200 poems in total, though __________ were published while she was alive.","opts":["all","few","little","every"],"pts":2.0,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"Emily Dickson은 1200편 이상의 시를 집필하였으나 오히려 살아있는 동안에는 거의 출판된 작품이 없었다는 내용이다. 부정의 의미로 가산명사를 수식할 수 있는 ②few가 정답이다."},{"q":13,"stem":"It was later found that Ben Johnson had taken an illegal drug, which led to __________ from Olympic sports.","opts":["be banning","him banning","he is banned","his being banned"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":4,"ex":"동명사의 어법을 묻는 문제이다. 전치사 to 다음에 [의미상의 주어(소유격/목적격) + 동명사]가 필요하며 ‘올림픽 경기 참가를 금지당했다’는 의미의 수동태가 필요하므로 ④his being banned가 정답이다. 보기 ①, ②는 능동태로 의미상 맞지 않는다."},{"q":14,"stem":"Professors are able to share their experiences and offer valuable insights into __________ studying a specific major requires in terms of skills, abilities, and effort.","opts":["how","that","what","whether"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"전치사 into의 목적어 역할을 하는 명사절이 필요하다. 접속사와 동사 requires의 목 적어의 역할을 함께 할 수 있는 ③what이 정답이다."},{"q":15,"stem":"Anita Roddick opened the first branch of The Body Shop in her hometown of Brighton, England. When she first opened, ①neighboring business owners and shop owners made bets among themselves on how long the store would last. Less amused ②was the owners of local funeral parlors who insisted she ③change the shop's name. No one, they complained, would hire a funeral director ④located near a place called \"The Body Shop.\" She stuck to her guns and the name stayed.","opts":["neighboring business","was the","change the","located near"],"pts":3.0,"inline":true,"sec":3,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"Anita Roddick이 오픈한 The Body Shop을 인근에 위치한(located) 장례업자들은 반기지 않았고 상점 이름을 바꿀 것(change)을 주장하였다는 내용이다. Less amused was the owners ... 는 도치구문으로 주어(the owners)가 복수이므로 동사 ②was는 were로 수정되어야 한다. 동사 insisted의 목적어절에는 [주어 + (should) 동사]의 구조가 사용되므로 ③change는 올바른 형태이다."},{"q":16,"stem":"The subscription service offers customers products that are ①tailored to their own personal needs and desires. This kind of treatment makes customers feel special and ②deepens their connection to the brand. In a retail environment where customers are faced with a dizzying array of products, this kind of service can combat ③which has been referred to as “the paralysis of choice.” In other words, the service makes decisions for consumers who may have difficulty making decisions for ④themselves.","opts":["tailored to","deepens their","which has","themselves."],"pts":2.5,"inline":true,"sec":3,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"③번의 자리에는 동사 combat의 목적어(절) 역할과 “has been referred to as ~” 의 주어 역할을 모두 하는 단어가 필요하다. 따라서 ③which는 what으로 수정되어야한다."},{"q":17,"stem":"To have any effect, placebos must look like real medical treatments. If patients know that they are taking a(n) __________ substance, then the illusion is ruined and it will have no effect.","opts":["inert","natural","medical","essential"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"플라시보(위약)는 실제 의약효과가 있는 것처럼 보여야 그 효력이 발생된다. 환자들이 ‘효력이 없는’ 물질을 복용하고 있다는 것을 안다면, 약효과에 대한 환상을 기대하 기 어렵다는 의미로 ① inert ‘비활성의, 활동력이 없는’이 정답이다."},{"q":18,"stem":"Consider what happens when you bite into a chili pepper. You think you have a volcano in your mouth, with explosions going off from lips to gums to tongue and throat. You break into a sweat and reach for your water glass to put out the fire. (It is a pointless exercise because capsaicin is barely soluble in water. The best thing is to drink milk because casein, one of the proteins in milk, specifically and directly __________ the effects of capsaicin.) Your eyes water and your nasal passages flood.","opts":["verifies","maximizes","counteracts","exacerbates"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"칠레 고추를 먹고 나서 캡사이신이 일으키는 맵고 얼얼한 입속의 열기를 없애려고할 때 우유의 casein이라는 단백질 성분이 캡사이신의 효과를 중화시킬 수 있다는 내용으로 빈칸에는 ‘중화하다’는 뜻을 가진 ③counteract가 적절하다."},{"q":19,"stem":"The fishermen in the Grand Banks of Newfoundland dragged their nets over the bottom of the sea, catching many kinds of unwanted fish in their nets. There was a lot of waste, and the action of the nets degraded the environment. People simply turned a blind eye to this situation, which existed for hundreds of years. Eventually, biologists who were studying the cod population began to warn of future problems. They argued that rational outcome of continuing in this way would be ______________________________.","opts":["the unrequired catch of fish","the removal of a lot of waste","the collapse of the cod fisheries","the destruction of the fishing nets"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"어부들이 그물을 사용해서 바다 바닥을 훑어 물고기를 포획할 때 원하지 않는 물고 기를 잡아들여서 쓰레기가 생기고, 환경을 악화시킨다. 생물학자들은 결국 이러한 행 위가 지속되면 대구 어장의 붕괴를 초래할 것이라고 경고한다는 내용으로 빈칸은 ③the collapse of the cod fisheries(대구 어장의 붕괴)가 정답이다."},{"q":20,"stem":"After his best friend moved, my son went through a very difficult time. Children react very differently from adults when things don't go well. For kids, negative reactions can include inattentiveness, hyperactivity, and acting out ― yelling, hitting, and generally being difficult to control. (A) , my son did not hit those depths, but he did have trouble sleeping, his attention was poor, and he was sad a lot of the time. (B) , this hit his friend as well, who was perhaps even more seriously upset and, being extroverted, was even more prone to acting out.","opts":["(A) Therefore (B) Similarly","(A) Fortunately (B) Of course","(A) However (B) For instance","(A) Indeed (B) Moreover"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"가장 친한 친구가 이사 가고 아들은 어려운 시기를 보냈다는 내용이다. 어린이들은 이런 경우에 다양한 부정적인 반응을 보여주는데, ‘다행히’ 내 아들은 밑바닥까지 타 격을 받지는 않았지만, 집중력 저하와 불면, 슬픔의 시간을 보냈다. ‘물론’ 이것은 아들 친구에게도 매우 심각하게 영향을 주었다. 따라서 빈칸에는 ②(A) Fortunately (B) Of course가 가장 적절하다."},{"q":21,"stem":"Since Alice was not the typical entrepreneur, she saw no disadvantages to starting her company with almost no finances. To save money, she bottled her cosmetics in the same inexpensive plastic containers hospitals use for urine samples, encouraging her customers to bring the containers back for refills. Because Alice couldn't afford to have labels printed, she hand printed them herself with the help of some friends. Her packaging couldn't have turned out better if she'd planned it that way. With the ____________ packaging, her product now had the same natural image as the cosmetics themselves.","opts":["sturdy","improvised","fragile","redeemable"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"Alice는 사업가로서 자금을 절약하기 위해 비싸지 않은 플라스틱병을 화장품 용기로 사용했고 라벨을 프린트할 자금 여유가 없어서 손으로 직접 썼다. 그 포장은 더 좋은 결과를 낳았으며, 이러한 즉흥적인 포장 제작은 화장품 자체와 함께 자연적인 이미지를 제공했다는 내용으로 빈칸에는 ‘즉흥적으로 만들어진’의 뜻을 지닌 ②improvised 가 적당하다."},{"q":22,"stem":"\"I am meeting a new doctor tomorrow. I hope he is qualified. Well, before I meet the doctor, I will have to see a nurse. I hope she is friendly.\" Can you see something wrong with the language above? People who favor gender-neutral language would immediately see a problem. Gender-neutral language tries to take away ____________ that certain professions are masculine and others feminine. In gender-neutral language, one would say: \"I am meeting a new doctor tomorrow. I hope he or she is qualified. Well, before I meet the doctor, I will have to see a nurse. I hope he or she is friendly.\"","opts":["trends","genders","demands","assumptions"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":4,"ex":"성을 구별해서 의사를 he로, 간호사를 she로 지칭하는 대신 he or she와 같이 성적 구별이 없는 언어는 특정 직업이 남성적이고, 다른 직업은 여성적이라는 ‘가정’을 없 애려고 노력한다는 내용이다. 빈칸에는 ‘가정, 가설’을 의미하는 ④assumptions가 적 당하다. 내용상 ①trends(추세, 동향), ②genders(성), ③demands(요구사항)는 적당하지 않다."},{"q":23,"stem":"In most people's brains, each of the senses is activated separately. That is, when you hear something, your sense of hearing is activated; when you see something, your sense of sight is activated, and so on. In the brain of someone with synesthesia, however, two or more senses are activated simultaneously. For example, a synesthete's sense of sight and hearing might be hooked together; as a result, whenever the synesthete hears a particular sound, she or he also sees a particular color. Thus, the synesthete might say that the sound of a doorbell is blue. This is not the same as a poet using language intentionally to excite the imagination of the reader. The synesthete is not making it up. The sensation of \"hearing\" a color __________________.","opts":["is the perception of sound when no actual sound is present","is as real to the synesthete as seeing a color is to you","comes from multiple sensory experiences of reading a poem","occurs when the synesthete voluntarily associates a sound with a sense of sight"],"pts":3.0,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"대부분의 사람들은 감각이 각각 분리되어 활성화되지만 synesthete(공감각자)는 두 개 이상의 감각이 동시에 활성화된다. 즉, 현관벨의 소리를 들을 때 특정 색을 함께 본다. 당신이 색상을 보는 것만큼이나 공감각자는 색상을 “듣는” 감각은 만들어 내는 것이 아니라 실질적인 경험이다. 그러므로 ②가 가장 적절하다."},{"q":24,"stem":"In 1964, Kitty Genovese was murdered in New York City. Reportedly, none of the 38 witnesses called the police or tried to help her, which was very disturbing to psychologists, among others. Since then, researchers have tried to understand the “bystander effect,” in other words, the __________ of onlookers to take action.","opts":["tendency","eagerness","reluctance","commitment"],"pts":2.0,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"뉴욕시에서 Kitty Genovese가 살해되었는데, 38명의 증인들 중 누구도 경찰에 연락 하거나 그녀를 도우려고 하지 않았다. 심리학자들은 이 현상을 ‘방관자효과’ 즉 방관 자가 행동을 취하기 ‘꺼리는’ 현상으로 이해하려고 한다. 빈칸에는 ‘마음이 내키지 않 음, 꺼림’이라는 의미를 가진 ③reluctance가 정답이다."},{"q":25,"stem":"Despite the early potential of the prodigies, it is difficult to know what will happen when they grow up. We still do not know exactly what genius really is, though many experts have tried to define it. The most famous predictor of intelligence is the Intelligence Quotient (IQ) test. It was developed by French psychologist Alfred Binet in the early twentieth century. However, many experts now confirm that this type of intelligence test ____________________. Most people who score exceptionally high on intelligence tests as children never do anything particularly exceptional with their lives.","opts":["is still not conducted","should never be underrated","predicts intelligence of adults","only tells one side of the story"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":4,"ex":"영재들은 초기 잠재력에도 불구하고, 그들이 성장했을 때에는 특별히 뛰어나지 않았 다는 내용이다. 우리는 영재를 아직 정확하게 규명하지 못하며, 전문가들은 지능을 예측하는 검사도 ‘한 측면만을 보여준다’며 검사의 한계점을 보여주었다. 따라서 빈칸 에는 ④only tells one side of the story가 적절하다."},{"q":26,"stem":"Moreland and Beach conducted the research to investigate ______________________________.","opts":["the intention of the research assistant who attended class the most","the effect of familiarity on decreasing feelings of isolation","how physical surroundings affect relationships among people","the connection between repeated exposure to a person and the evaluation of him or her"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":0,"a":4,"ex":"두 연구자가 4명의 연구조교에게 한 학기 동안 각각 15번, 10번, 5번, 0번 수업에 참석하도록 한 후 학기 말에 교실에 있는 학생들에게 4명의 연구조교에 대한 선호도를 평가하게 한다. 이는 누군가와의 반복된 접촉과 그 사람에 대한 평가가 관련이 있 는지를 파악하기 위한 연구이므로 ④가 정답이다."},{"q":27,"stem":"Choose the most suitable position of the sentence below in the above passage. I tried to correct myself as I turned through the air, putting my hands wide apart.","opts":["(A)","(B)","(C)","(D)"],"pts":2.0,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":1,"a":3,"ex":"한 다이버가 다이빙보드에서 점프를 하기 직전의 동작을 설명하는 글이다. (A) 다이 빙보드를 발로 딛고 뛰어오르며 팔과 어깨를 들어 올렸을 때 (B) 보드에 너무 가까워서 손을 부딪칠 수 있다는 것을 즉각적으로 알게 된다 (C) 그리고 나서 이상한 소리를 듣고 몸을 제대로 가눌 수 없다는 것을 느낀다 (D) 이후에 보드에 머리를 부딪힌 것을 알게 되었다는 내용이다. 그러므로 인용한 예문은 내가 공중에서 회전할 때 팔을 넓게 뻗으며 부딪치지 않으려 자세를 교정했다는 내용이므로 제대로 몸을 가눌 수 없다는 내용 앞 위치인 ③(C)가 적당하다."},{"q":28,"stem":"Which can be inferred from the passage?","opts":["Keys suffered from heart disease and tried to find the cure for it.","Keys wished the food served in American-Italian restaurants were more like traditional Mediterranean fare.","Americans tend to go to extremes when it comes to healthy eating.","There are many Italian dishes which are very hard to translate into English."],"pts":3.0,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":2,"a":2,"ex":"전통적 지중해식 식사법의 옹호자이자 홍보자로 잘 알려진 생리학자의 이야기이다. 이 학자는 지중해 지역에서는 심장병이 드물다는 것을 알게 되고 죽기 직전까지 활발히 연구를 하였다. 그는 한 인터뷰에서 미국인들이 접하는 이탈리아 음식이 전통적 지중해식 음식과 거의 관련이 없다는 것을 애석해 하였다. 따라서 문맥상 ‘미국화된 이탈리안 음식이 전통적 지중해식 음식에 더 가까워지기를 바란다’는 내용을 유추할 수 있으므로 ②가 정답이다."},{"q":29,"stem":"Which is implied in the passage?","opts":["Thailand insists that chili is exclusively Thai.","Thailand is the largest importer of food ingredients in the world.","Other small fruits are more consumed than chili peppers in Thailand.","The defining feature of Thai cuisine is achieved by the good use of chili peppers."],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":3,"a":4,"ex":"태국은 고추의 원산지는 아니지만 많은 양을 소비하기 때문에 오히려 원산지인 것처 럼 보일 수도 있다는 내용의 글이다. 특히 가공되지 않은 신선한 고추를 잘 사용하는 것이 가장 큰 특징이라는 내용이 나오므로 ④가 정답이다."},{"q":30,"stem":"Which is closest in meaning to the underlined part?","opts":["America is rich because of scrap.","Saudi Arabia sells scrap to China.","America is the top exporter of scrap.","American exports to China are complex."],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":4,"a":3,"ex":"폐기물은 미국이 중국으로 수출하는 품목 중 3번째로 많은 양을 차지한다는 내용이다. 이러한 내용을 잘 보여주는 폐기물 처리 관련 기관의 한 관계자의 말이 인용된다. ‘We are the Saudi Arabia of scrap’은 사우디아라비아가 최대 원유 생산국이자 수출국이듯이 미국도 최대 폐기물 수출국인 면에서 보면 사우디아라비아와 다를 것이 없다. 따라서 ③이 정답이다."},{"q":31,"stem":"Which is true according to the passage?","opts":["May Sinclair originated a new literary technique, stream of consciousness.","Structure in literature makes the story less believable to readers.","Authors use stream of consciousness to portray a flow of character's inner thoughts.","The most successful writers revolutionized their novels by adopting stream of consciousness."],"pts":3.0,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":5,"a":3,"ex":"의식의 흐름은 19세기 중반에서 후반에 등장한 기법으로 등장인물의 본질에 가장 가까이 다가가기 위하여 내적인 생각과 느낌을 적나라하게 표현하는 것이 특징이라는 내용이다. ①,②,④는 글의 내용과 다르고 ③은 ‘등장인물의 내적 생각과 의식의 흐름을 잘 묘사한다’는 내용이 언급되었으므로 정답이다."},{"q":32,"stem":"Which is NOT suggested about CAM treatments?","opts":["They have less effect when used with conventional remedies.","They treat the whole patient rather than only the symptoms.","Some patients can feel worse before completely cured.","They involve triggering the body's natural defense."],"pts":3.0,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":6,"a":1,"ex":"전통 치료법과 대체 치료법을 설명하는 글이다. 급성 질병에는 전통 치료법이 사용 되고 만성 질병에는 대체 치료법이 더 선호된다. 대체 치료법은 통증을 줄이는 것 외 에도 전반적인 건강 기능을 향상시켜 줄 수 있다. 일거양득의 효과를 위해 두 치료법은 함께 사용된다는 내용이 나오므로 ④가 정답이다."},{"q":33,"stem":"Which proverb is the most suitable for the blank?","opts":["set a thief to catch a thief","a bird never flew on one wing","the enemy of my enemy is my friend","when the going gets tough, the tough get going"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":6,"a":1,"ex":"동종 치료법은 말 그대로 비슷한 성질의 것으로 질병을 치료할 수 있다는 ‘이열치 열’ 의미이므로 ①도둑은 도둑으로 잡는다는 속담이 가장 적절하다."},{"q":34,"stem":"Choose the one that best completes the blanks.","opts":["(A) assess (B) humble","(A) reveal (B) sympathetic","(A) cover (B) respected","(A) distribute (B) talented"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":7,"a":3,"ex":"단어 sincere(진실한, 거짓 없는)의 어원을 설명하는 지문이다. 예전에 도기에 생긴 갈라진 금을 가리기 위해 밀랍을 사용한 도공들과 그렇지 않았던 도공들이 있었다. 훌륭한 도공들이 ‘밀랍(cero) 없이(sin)‘ 도기를 만든 것에서 sincere라는 단어가 유래 되었다. 따라서 (A)에는 cover(가리다), (B)에는 respected(훌륭한, 평판이 좋은)가 가장 적절하다."},{"q":35,"stem":"Which is the best title of the passage?","opts":["The Interesting Story of a Word","The Evolution of Latin Language","The Importance of Being Honest","The Development of Ancient Pottery"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":7,"a":1,"ex":"sincere라는 단어의 흥미로운 어원에 관한 이야기이므로 단락의 제목으로 ①The Interesting Story of a Word가 가장 적절하다."},{"q":36,"stem":"Which is the most suitable for the blank?","opts":["astute","transforming","hostile","unsuspecting"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":8,"a":4,"ex":"남아메리카와 아프리카에 서식하는 거미인 bolas spider는 먹잇감을 사냥하기 위해 페로몬을 사용한다. 암컷 나방이 발산하는 것과 유사한 페로몬을 내뿜어 먹잇감인 수 컷 나방을 유인하고 수컷 나방은 이 사실을 모르고 bolas spider에게 다가가게 된다. 따라서, 빈칸에는 ④unsuspecting(의심하지 않는, 수상히 여기지 않는)이 가장 적절하다."},{"q":37,"stem":"Which is suggested in the passage?","opts":["The Large Blue caterpillar has a unique way of protecting itself.","The Large Blue caterpillar releases pheromones that repel ants.","The ants get other species to take care of their young.","The bolas spider uses pheromones to attract female moths."],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":8,"a":1,"ex":"Large Blue caterpillar는 애벌레 단계에서 자신을 보호하기 위해 개미와 유사한 페 로몬을 발산하여 성충인 나비가 될 때까지 개미집에서 자란다. 따라서, ①의 the Large Blue caterpillar는 자신을 보호하는 독특한 방식이 있다가 답으로 적절하다. ②의 개미를 쫓아버리는 페로몬을 Large Blue caterpillar가 내뿜는다는 것은 단락의 내용과 반대된다. 또한, 개미들이 다른 종의 곤충들에게 어린 개미 돌보기를 시킨다는 내용은 본문에 없으므로 ③도 정답으로 적절하지 않다. The bolas spider는 페로 몬을 사용하여 수컷 나방을 유인하므로 암컷 나방을 유인한다고 한 ④도 정답으로 적 절하지 않다."},{"q":38,"stem":"Choose the appropriate order of the paragraphs.","opts":["(A) - (B) - (C)","(A) - (C) - (B)","(B) - (C) - (A)","(C) - (B) - (A)"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":9,"a":4,"ex":"(A)는 서구와는 달리 일본에서는 광고를 제작할 때 제품 자체에 관한 설명보다는 그 제품에 대한 긍정적인 느낌이나 분위기를 전달하려고 한다. (B)는 광고 회사들은 각 나라의 커뮤니케이션 스타일에 맞게 글로벌 광고를 제작한다. (C)는 각 나라의 언어와 문화가 다르기 때문에 글로벌 광고 제작이 어렵다는 내용이다. 이러한 내용을 고 려하여 세 문단의 순서를 정리하면 언어와 문화가 다름으로 인해 발생한 글로벌 광고의 어려움을 다룬 (C)가 가장 앞에 나와야 하며, 이러한 문제를 해결하기 위해 글로 벌 광고를 제작할 때는 기존 광고의 번역이 아닌 각 나라의 문화와 커뮤니케이션 스 타일에 맞는 새로운 광고를 제작하는 것을 다룬 (B)가 그 다음에 와야 한다. 마지막으로 (B)의 후반부의 내용에 맞는 국가들의 예시가 (A)의 전반부와 연결되므로 단락의 순서는 (C)-(B)-(A)가 되어야 한다."},{"q":39,"stem":"Which is NOT true according to the passage?","opts":["Ads showing the features of the product are often successful in Western culture.","Different countries use different styles of communicating.","Unintended meanings can be carried in translation.","The Nova campaign failed in Latin America because of the goal of the ads."],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":9,"a":4,"ex":"Chevrolet의 광고가 실패한 원인은 오역으로 인해 생긴 문제이므로 ④는 지문의 내 용과 다르다. ①은 서구권에서는 제품의 특징을 잘 보여주는 광고를 하고, ②각 나라는 커뮤니케이션 스타일이 다르고 ③번역시 의도하지 않은 의미가 전달될 수도 있다는 것은 지문의 내용과 부합된다."},{"q":40,"stem":"What is the passage mainly about?","opts":["The latest global advertising trends","The difficulties of global advertising","The importance of advertising in marketing","The way to create the right kind of message"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":9,"a":2,"ex":"글로벌 광고를 제작할 때 각 나라의 문화와 언어에 따라 다른 광고 전략을 사용해야 함을 설명하고 있으므로 ②글로벌 마케팅의 어려움(The difficulties of global)이 주 제를 적절하게 나타낸다. 기타 ①최신 글로벌 광고 동향이나 ③광고의 중요성, ④적 절한 메시지를 만드는 방법에 관한 설명은 지문에 없으므로 정답으로 적절하지 않다."}]},"2026":{"sections":["Choose the one that is closest in meaning to the underlined word(s).","Choose the one that best fills in the blank.","Choose the one that most grammatically completes the sentence.","Choose the one that is grammatically INCORRECT.","Choose the one(s) that best complete(s) the sentence.","Read the following passages and answer the questions."],"passages":["Israel Mensah, 20, explains how he makes his living. (A) Each day, scrap sellers bring loads of old electronics. (B) Mensah’s friends and family buy a few computers or TVs. They break them apart to remove valuable metals and wires, as well as any parts that can be resold. Then they burn the plastic covering off the wire and sell it. (C) “The gas goes to your nose, and you feel something in your head,” Mensah says as he knocks his fist against his head. (D) “Then you get sick in your head and your chest. But I don’t bother.”","As much as I found the trip exhilarating, I would not say it is for everyone. Eco-tourism means responsible, low-impact travel, and generally involves some degree of ‘roughing-it.’ This trip is no exception. Three of the five nights were spent in hammocks, which did not suit everyone’s natural contours. You must not be averse to sun, sweat, mosquitoes, or bathing in rivers with little or no privacy. At $1,500 per person for the week-long trip it’s an excellent deal, but still prohibitively expensive for some people. If you can afford it, and don’t mind a few ants in your pants, this trip will provide you with an incredibly unique experience that I guarantee you will never forget.","One cloudless midsummer day, Andrew Parker, an evolutionary biologist, knelt in the baking red sand of an Australian desert and gently placed the right back leg of a thorny devil into a dish of water. The thorny devil, a small lizard that has learned to survive in the intense heat of the Australian desert, has a secret that fascinated Parker. “Look, look! ” he exclaimed. “Its back is completely drenched! ” Sure enough, in less than a minute, water from the dish had traveled up the lizard’s leg, across its skin, and into its mouth. It was, in essence, drinking through its foot. The thorny devil can also do this when standing on damp sand—a vital competitive advantage in the desert. Parker had come here to solve the riddle of precisely how it does this, not from purely biological interest, but with a concrete purpose in mind: to make a device to help people collect water in the desert.","Glass had already become a serious business by the dawn of the Roman empire. The writer Petronius recounts the tale of a craftsman presenting Emperor Tiberius with a piece of allegedly unbreakable glass. Tiberius asked the craftsman, “Does anyone else know how to blow glass like this?” “No,” the craftsman replied, thinking he’d made it big. Without warning, Tiberius had the man beheaded. Although Tiberius’s motives remain mysterious, one can imagine such an invention would have disrupted Rome’s important glass industry, the first of its kind.","Speaking a second language allows people to learn about another culture through the special words and phrases in that language. For example, a person who speaks North American English knows the expression meat and potatoes. If we say someone is a meat and potatoes kind of person, it means that person does not like special food. Therefore, it also tells us that in this culture, meat and potatoes—not rice, not pasta, not fish—______________________________. Likewise, through the baseball expressions to hit a home run (to do something that is very successful) or to strike out (to fail completely), we learn that the sport of baseball is important in North American culture. Thus, becoming bilingual can increase knowledge of not only a new language but also a new culture.","With great progress often comes great concern. As mammal cloning becomes more commonplace, people are beginning to wonder if human cloning is next. While the vast majority of scientists find the possibility ethically unacceptable, the technology could also fall into the wrong hands. Some fears of human cloning rest in the possibility of creating a flawless human, or a master race, by weeding out undesirable traits, such as inherited mental and physical disabilities. Others express the worry that human uniqueness will ultimately be wiped out by the procedure, and that we will become mere cattle ourselves.","From about 1300 to 800 B.C., the Lapita people colonized islands that stretch over millions of square kilometers, including the Solomon Islands, Santa Cruz Islands, Vanuatu, Fiji, New Caledonia, and Samoa. Then, for unknown reasons, they stopped. There was an interval of around 1,000 years before the civilization of the Polynesians, descendants of the Lapita, launched a new period of exploration. Then they outdid the Lapita with unbelievable feats of navigation, expanding the boundaries of their oceanic world until it was many times the size of that explored by their ancestors. Their colonies included the Cook Islands, French Polynesia, Easter Island, and Hawaii, eventually reaching South America around 1000 A.D.","Long ago I believed that survival meant having enough equipment to make fire, build shelter, and trap animals to eat in the wild. Then I kept coming across cases in which someone had survived without any equipment. In other cases, someone had all the right tools, but wasn’t able to survive. Why was this? Studying survival stories, I realized that how well people cope with adversity can be more important than any type of equipment or training. A person’s individual character is an essential element in the equation.","Synthetic textiles have come a long way since nylon. Kevlar, a textile that is stronger than steel, is used in bulletproof vests and in ropes used by astronauts. Other high-tech fibers can resist very high temperatures—perfect for firefighters and race-car drivers. Not all companies are __________ about their products for fear of having their ideas stolen. However, Huges Vinchon, an executive at Dubar-Warneton, a manufacturer of high-tech textiles in France, is happy to display some of his company’s amazing synthetic fibers his company creates. There is an oil-eating textile that absorbs five times its weight in oil, and is perfect for cleaning up oil spills. Another absorbs vibrations. “Can you imagine a motorboat you can’t hear?” he says. There is also an ordinary-looking cloth bag that is completely water soluble, according to Vinchon. “It’s strong enough to carry heavy objects. But if I dip it in boiling water, it disappears.”","To call Leonardo da Vinci an excellent painter is like labelling William Shakespeare a clever wordsmith. He was a true genius, recognized in his own time and idolized in ours. His paintings are as secret and seductive as himself, done with the hand of an angel, the intellect of a scientist, and the soul of a romantic. His drawings are among the most beautiful ever made; his most treasured painting, the Mona Lisa, is undoubtedly the most famous in the world.","(A) Water consumption in the city of Durban is now less than it was in 2016, even as 800,000 more people have received service. Through sensible water use, Durban’s conservation measures paid for themselves within a year. Neil Macleod has assured the city that no new dams will be needed in the coming decades, despite the expected addition of about 300,000 inhabitants. (B) In South Africa, Neil Macleod took over as head of Durban Metro Water Services in 2012. The situation he found was a catastrophe. Durban had one million people living in the city and another 1.5 million people who lived in poverty just outside it. Macleod and his engineers determined that the entire city was rife with broken water pipes, leaky toilets, and faulty plumbing whereby 42 percent of the region’s water was simply being wasted. (C) Neil Macleod’s crew began repairing and replacing water pipes. They put water meters on residences, replaced eight-liter toilets with four-liter models, and changed wasteful showers and water faucets. To ensure that the poor would receive a basic supply of water, Macleod installed tanks in homes and apartments to provide 190 liters of water a day free to each household."],"questions":[{"q":1,"stem":"Certain philosophers claim that suicide in any form is deplorable.","opts":["punishable","ineligible","conceivable","reprehensible"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":0,"psg":null,"a":4,"ex":"deplorable은 ‘개탄스러운, 비난받아 마땅한’이라는 의미이다. 따라서 보기에 나온 단어들 중에서 ‘비난받아 마땅한, 규탄할 만한’을 뜻하는 reprehensible이 가장 의미가 유사하다. punishable (벌 줄 수 있는, 처벌할 만한), ineligible (자격이 없는), conceivable (상상 가능한, 있을 법한) 등은 답으로 적합하지 않다."},{"q":2,"stem":"It is against the law to meddle with any of this building’s smoke detectors.","opts":["tamper","smuggle","replicate","distribute"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":0,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"meddle with는 ‘~에 함부로 손대다, 간섭하다’라는 의미이다. 따라서 보기에 나온 단어들 중에서 ‘~을 훼손하다, 조작하다, 함부로 만지다’를 뜻하는 temper (with)가 가장 의미가 유사하다. smuggle (밀수하다), replicate (복제하다), distribute (배포하다) 등은 답으로 적합하지 않다."},{"q":3,"stem":"In Gravity, the highly successful science fiction film directed by Alfonso Cuaron, two astronauts are stranded in space, and they have no way of contacting Earth.","opts":["floated","trapped","distressed","suffocated"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":0,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"stranded는 ‘(수단 따위가 다하여) 꼼짝 못하게 된’이라는 의미이다. 따라서 보기에 나온 단어들 중에서 ‘(빠져나올 수 없게) 갇힌, 고립된’을 뜻하는 trapped가 가장 의 미가 유사하다. floated (떠돌게 된), distressed (괴로운, 불안한), suffocated (질식한, 숨이 막히게 된) 등은 답으로 적합하지 않다."},{"q":4,"stem":"Initially, family feuds and kin-based mercantile associations were very common, but over time, the propensity for families to take retribution into their own hands abated.","opts":["admiration","expectation","inclination","nomination"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":0,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"propensity는 ‘~하려는 성향, 경향’이라는 의미이다. 따라서 보기에 나온 단어들 중에서 ‘성향, 경향’을 뜻하는 inclination이 가장 의미가 유사하다. admiration (감탄, 존경), expectation (기대), nomination (지명, 추천) 등은 답으로 적합하지 않다."},{"q":5,"stem":"The board of governors of the school weighed in with the proposal, and it was carried by a unanimous vote.","opts":["offered","circulated","installed","measured"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":0,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"weighed in with는 ‘(의견을) 제시하다, 제안하다’라는 의미이다. 따라서 보기에 나 온 단어들 중에서 ‘제의하다, 제시하다, 제출하다’를 뜻하는 offered가 가장 의미가 유사하다. circulated ((문서 등을) 회람하다), installed (설치하다), measured (측정하다, 평가하다) 등은 답으로 적합하지 않다."},{"q":6,"stem":"During the years of ______________ in the United States, it was very difficult for African-Americans to travel. Throughout the United States, and especially in the South, most hotels and restaurants did not allow African-Americans to enter.","opts":["reconstruction","segregation","emancipation","deterioration"],"pts":2.0,"inline":false,"sec":1,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"흑인들이 여행하기 어렵고, 특히 남부에서 호텔·식당 출입이 제한되었다는 내용으로 미국의 인종 분리 정책 시대를 설명하고 있다. 따라서 보기에 나온 단어들 중에서 ‘분리, 차단’을 뜻하는 segregation이 정답이다. reconstruction (재건, 부흥), emancipation (해방), deterioration (악화, 쇠퇴) 등은 답으로 적합하지 않다."},{"q":7,"stem":"Since our ancestors discovered the controlled use of fire, biomass has played a prominent role in global energy production and has recently been ___________ as the answer to our ever diminishing fossil fuel supply.","opts":["heralded","analyzed","compensated","fabricated"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":1,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"바이오매스가 최근 감소하고 있는 화석 연료 자원의 해결책으로 주목받다의 의미이다. 따라서 보기에 나온 단어들 중에서 ‘예고하다, 선도하다’를 뜻하는 heralded가 정 답이다. analyzed (분석하다), compensated (보상하다), fabricated (꾸며내다, 날조하다) 등은 답으로 적합하지 않다."},{"q":8,"stem":"These countries already contain a(n) _____________ portion of the world’s population, around 43 percent of all the people on earth.","opts":["variable","sizeable","negligible","ungraspable"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":1,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"전 세계 인구의 43%라면 전 세계의 인구의 상당한 부분을 차지한다고 말하는 것이 가장 자연스럽다. 따라서 보기에 나온 단어들 중에서 ‘상당한, 꽤 큰’을 뜻하는 sizeable이 정답이다. variable (변하기 쉬운), negligible (무시해도 좋은, 사소한), ungraspable (이해하기 어려운, 파악하기 힘든) 등은 답으로 적합하지 않다."},{"q":9,"stem":"Modern technology now makes it possible for people who live on the coast to know in advance if there is the possibility of ____________________.","opts":["a hurricane hits their region","their region hit by a hurricane","a hurricane hitting their region","hitting their region by a hurricane"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"동명사의 어법을 묻는 문제로 전치사 of 뒤에 동명사의 의미상의 주어와 동명사가 나온 a hurricane hitting their region (허리케인이 그 지역을 강타할 가능성)이 정답이다. 보기 ① a hurricane hits their region은 전치사 뒤에 완전한 절이 왔기 때문에 정답이 될 수 없고 ② hitting their region by a hurricane은 능동의 동명사구 뒤에 수동의 의미인 by a hurricane이 와서 정답이 될 수 없다. ④ their region hit by a hurricane은 문법적으로는 가능하지만 ‘허리케인에 의해 이미 피해를 입은 지역’이라는 의미이므로 현대의 기술이 미리 알 수 있게 해준다는 문장의 전체적인 의미에 맞지 않으므로 정답이 될 수 없다."},{"q":10,"stem":"The word cult is used to describe a wide variety of groups, some of ___________ have a religious or quasi-religious basis.","opts":["all","what","them","which"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":4,"ex":"전치사 + 관계대명사의 구조를 묻는 문제이다. 앞의 절과 some of ______로 시작되는 뒤의 절을 연결할 수 있는 역할은 관계대명사이다. 따라서 ④ which가 정답이다. ① some of all, ③ some of them은 접속사 역할을 하는 단어가 없으므로 문법적으로 맞지 않다. ② what은 선행사가 있는 관계절에는 사용할 수 없다."},{"q":11,"stem":"__________________ with listing renewable forms of energy, people tend to mention solar, wind, or hydro.","opts":["Tasking","To task","When tasked","Having tasked"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"‘~을 하도록 맡겨졌을 때, ~을 하라는 과제를 받으면’을 의미하는 ③ When tasked 가 정답이다. When (people are) tasked with ~의 부사절이 분사구문이 되어 When tasked가 된 구조이다. ‘일을 부과하다’를 의미하는 타동사 task 뒤에 목적어가 없으므로 능동의 형태로 쓴 ① Tasking, ② To task, ④ Having tasked는 정답이 될 수 없다."},{"q":12,"stem":"Those ____________ to the mandatory volunteering believe that the term mandatory volunteering is a contradiction.","opts":["opposed","who opposed","are opposed","that are opposing"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"문장에서 주어 역할을 하는 Those + (형용사/분사) + to ~ 의 구조로 ‘~에 반대하는 사람들’이라는 의미로 ① opposed가 정답이다. Those와 opposed 사이에는 ‘주격 관계대명사 + be 동사’가 생략되어 있다고 볼 수 있다."},{"q":13,"stem":"A ticket in First Class can cost ______________ a ticket in Economy Class.","opts":["up to more twenty times than","as twenty times as much up to","up to twenty times as much as","twenty times up to more than"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"[up to + 배수사 + as 원급 as]의 구조이고 ‘최대 ~배 만큼’의 의미로 ③ up to twenty times as much as가 정답이다. ① up to more twenty times than, ② as twenty times as much up to, ④ twenty times as up to much as 모두 어순에 오 류가 있으므로 오답이다."},{"q":14,"stem":"In the past, people believed that alchemists could create seemingly magical transformations by studying metals and other natural elements. They applied their understanding of chemistry, astrology, and physics in the hope to create gold or extend life. However, alchemists went beyond _______________________ today by using mysticism and spiritual ideas.","opts":["that we think of science","which science we think of","we think of that as science","what we think of as science"],"pts":3.0,"inline":false,"sec":2,"psg":null,"a":4,"ex":"이 문장에 필요한 것은 전치사 뒤에 ‘~라고 생각하는 것’을 의미하는 선행사를 포함한 관계대명사 what이 이끄는 명사절이다. 따라서 ‘오늘날 우리가 과학이라고 생각하는 범위를 넘어’를 의미하는 ④ beyond what we think of as science가 정답이다. 전치사 뒤에는 that이 이끄는 절이나 완전한 절이 올 수 없으므로 ① that science we think of나 ③ we think of that as science는 정답이 될 수 없다. 선행사가 없는 경우 관계대명사 which는 사용할 수 없으므로 ② which science we think of도 정답이 될 수 없다."},{"q":15,"stem":"The Japanese eel ①added to the International Union for Conservation of Nature’s list with an endangered classification, ②meaning it has a high risk of becoming extinct. It ③has been hit by overfishing, habitat loss, and pollution. ④Despite these warnings, fishing quotas have been slow to change. Experts warn that without immediate, strong international cooperation, this iconic species could disappear within decades.","opts":["added to","meaning it","has been","Despite these"],"pts":2.5,"inline":true,"sec":3,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"The Japanese eel(일본뱀장어)은 문장의 주어이고, ‘International Union for Conservation of Nature 목록에 추가되었다’는 의미이므로 수동태의 동사가 필요하다. 따라서 ① added to는 was added to가 되어야 한다."},{"q":16,"stem":"Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart was a musical mastermind. For one thing, Mozart was a child prodigy who ①was playing the violin and piano by age four and composing by age six. Another reason that he is considered a genius is ②why he was able to create more than 600 compositions—including symphonies, chamber music, sonatas, and choral music—in his thirty-four-year lifetime. Additionally, he is said ③to have been able to compose entire symphonies in his head. He could imagine the sounds of all the different instruments without using a piano to ④help him compose. He was not only the best pianist of his day in Europe but also one of the top three or four violinists.","opts":["was playing","why he","to have","help him"],"pts":2.5,"inline":true,"sec":3,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"동사 is 뒤의 보어절을 이끄는 접속사로 적절한 것은 명사절 접속사 that으로 Another reason ... is that SV의 구조이다. ① was playing에서 playing은 접속사 and 뒤의 composing과 병렬관계이고, ③ to have been은 be said to have p.p.의 구조이고, ④ help him compose는 help + 목적어 + 동사원형의 구조이다."},{"q":17,"stem":"Product placement is a term that refers to the insertion of commercials in various forms of media. Product placements can appear in films, television programs, plays, music videos, video games, and books. Directors might take special care to show the logo of a brand of blue jeans, for example. (A) , a character may drink a particular brand of soda and sigh in satisfaction. Product placements are designed to be subtle, the goal being that the appearance of the product seems natural to the viewer. (B) , advertisers are able to send what are known as subliminal messages that inspire audiences to develop a preference for a product.","opts":["(A) Indeed (B) Eventually","(A) Therefore (B) Moreover","(A) In addition (B) However","(A) Alternatively (B) In this way"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":4,"ex":"(A)의 앞 문장에서는 청바지 로고를 보여주는 예를 들었고, 다음 문장은 또 다른 예 시(탄산음료를 마시며 만족)가 나오므로 ‘또 다른 예로’라는 의미가 있는 Alternatively 가 흐름상 자연스럽다. (B)의 앞 문장에서 PPL은 자연스럽게 보이도록 ‘미묘하게 (subtle) 설계’되고 (B) 다음은 ‘광고주는 잠재의식적 메시지(subliminal messages)를 전달할 수 있다’는 ‘결과’에 해당하는 내용이 나오므로 In this way (이런 방식으로) 가 가장 적절하다."},{"q":18,"stem":"A scientific hypothesis must be falsifiable. That is, you must be able to imagine a way to show that it is false, such as by giving an example showing that it is wrong. Of course, scientists do not show every hypothesis to be false—the important point is that ________________________. This is why personal opinions, such as “It is wrong to cheat on exams,” are not scientific—each person has a different idea about right and wrong. It is not possible to falsify opinions.","opts":["proving the hypothesis false is possible","identifying right and wrong is justifiable","demonstrating the process of falsification is unfeasible","providing many examples makes the hypothesis plausible"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"과학적 가설은 반증 가능해야 하며 (falsifiable) 이때 중요한 것은 과학적 가설은 틀 렸음을 증명할 수 있어야 한다는 의미가 되어야 한다. 다시 말해서 반증의 가능성이 열려 있어야 한다는 것이다. ② 옳고 그름을 판단하는 것이 타당해야 한다거나 ③ 반 증의 과정을 보여주는 것이 가능하지 않다거나 ④ 예시를 많이 보여주면 가정이 그럴 듯 해진다는 것은 반증과는 무관하다."},{"q":19,"stem":"When worry escalates, the result is fear. Everyone has experienced fear. A swimmer of only moderate skill might be afraid of swift waters; a child might fear dark. A hiker will probably feel fear when hearing the distinctive warning of a rattlesnake; a jogger might experience it when confronted with an angry dog. According to the author Norman Cousins, “Fear creates negative expectations. One tends to move in the direction of one’s expectations.” Fear causes the heart to race, the head to spin, the palms to sweat, the knees to buckle, and breathing to become labored. Its physical effects are such that _______________________________.","opts":["it is better not to confront fear","we should try to hold our emotion back","negative expectations proved to be wrong","the human body can’t withstand fear indefinitely"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":4,"ex":"빈 칸 앞의 문장에서는 공포(fear)로 인한 신체적 반응을 열거하고 있다. 그리고 지 문의 마지막 문장은 그 신체적 영향이 너무 큰 결과를 불러올 수 있다는 내용으로 마 무리 되어야 한다. 따라서 ‘인간의 신체는 공포를 무한히 견딜 수 없다’라는 의미가 가장 자연스럽다. ① 공포를 대면하지 않는 것이 더 낫다거나 ② 우리의 감정을 억눌 러야 한다거나 ③ 부정적 예상이 틀렸음이 판명되었다는 것은 문맥상 어울리지 않는다."},{"q":20,"stem":"There is the principle of _______________________. Giving off light can help summon the predator of your predator. Known as the ‘burglar alarm’ effect, this is especially useful for tiny life forms that cannot swim fast. For such beings, water is too viscous to allow a quick getaway—it would be like trying to swim through syrup. Instead, when threatened by a shrimp, for example, these organisms light up. The flashes attract larger fish that are better able to spot—and eat—the shrimp. The chief defense for these organisms is therefore not fight or flight—but light.","opts":["“every cloud has a silver lining”","“a good retreat is better than a fight”","“the enemy of my enemy is my friend”","“better to light a candle than curse the darkness”"],"pts":2.0,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"이 지문은 포식자(적)가 공격하면, 포식자의 적인 더 큰 포식자(적의 적)를 불러서 자신을 보호한다는 원리를 설명하고 있다. 따라서 빈 칸에는 ‘내 적(포식자)의 적(더 큰 포식자)은 내 편이다’라는 속담이 가장 적합하다. ① 쥐구멍에도 볕들 날이 있다, ② 싸우기 보다는 퇴각이 더 낫다, ④ 불평하기 보다는 문제를 해결하는 편이 더 낫 다는 것은 지문의 내용와 맞지 않다."},{"q":21,"stem":"The problem is that if prisons are made more pleasant places to be, this may assist in achieving the rehabilitation of some prisoners, but it may also mean that a prison sentence becomes less of a(n) __________ to those who may commit crimes.","opts":["deterrent","response","alternative","preference"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":1,"ex":"감옥을 더 쾌적하게 만들면 사회 복귀(rehabilitation)에 도움이 되지만 동시에 범죄를 저지르려는 사람들에게 감옥형은 오히려 범죄 억제 효과가 약해질 수 있다는 내용이다. 따라서 빈칸에는 deterrent(억제/제재)가 적절하다."},{"q":22,"stem":"In book publishing, many companies do not always scrutinize the information authors write. A best-selling book can make a lot of money, so some authors find it tempting to make up lies. In one famous case, a writer concocted a completely fictitious history about himself. The writing seemed credible, so most readers believed his story. However, the writer later was unable to document the facts in the book, and he was revealed as a fake, which provoked controversy for him and his publisher. Although the writer’s tale was not legitimate, many people still found it meaningful. Even these readers agree that they would rather not be left in the dark, ____________. They would rather be aware of any major alteration of facts that could turn a good true story into just a good story.","opts":["doubting who the real author is","unaware that there was a dispute","not realizing how great the story was","wondering whether or not a story is true"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":4,"ex":"이 단락의 주된 내용은 ‘작가가 거짓으로 이야기를 일부 꾸며내었지만, 의미 있는 내용이기 때문에 독자는 사실 여부를 가리기보다는 어느 부분에 사실과 다른 변경 (alteration)이 있었는지를 더 알고 싶어 한다.’이다. 따라서 빈칸에는 ‘진짜인지 아닌 지를 궁금해 하며’라는 의미를 가진’ ④가 가장 자연스럽다."},{"q":23,"stem":"There is a whole category of crime—corporate crime that is usually committed by people of high social status who work as company officials. Examples of corporate crime include disregard of safety in the workplace, the production of unsafe products, and violation of environmental regulations. Such crimes are committed without the obvious use of force, and the effect of the crime on the victims cannot be easily traced to the offender. The people who are involved in corporate crime often have a great deal of power that they use to avoid conviction. Much corporate crime escapes punishment. If a miner dies of lung disease, for example, it is _____________ to prove beyond a reasonable doubt that he died because the employer broke the law by not providing adequate safety in the mine.","opts":["unethical","difficult","necessary","sufficient"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"이 지문은 기업범죄를 정의하고 기업범죄의 예와 특징들을 설명하고 있다. 문맥상 마지막 문장은 ‘광부가 폐질환으로 죽었다 해도, 고용주가 적절한 안전조치를 하지 않아 법을 어겼기 때문에 광부가 죽었다는 것을 합리적 의심을 넘어 증명하기가 어렵다’가 되어야 하므로 ② difficult가 정답이다. 따라서 ① unethical (비윤리적인), ③ necessary (필요한), ④ sufficient (충분한)은 정답이 될 수 없다."},{"q":24,"stem":"Caffeine increases your pulse, which may lend you more physical strength for a while. But, experts caution, this effect may not be seen in habitual drinkers, whose bodies may have built up __________ to this substance.","opts":["immunity","expertise","tolerance","adaptation"],"pts":3.0,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":3,"ex":"습관적으로 커피를 마시는 사람들은 몸이 카페인에 익숙해져서(내성이 생겨서) 그 효과가 잘 나타나지 않을 수 있다는 의미이므로 ③ tolerance (내성)이 정답이다. 따 라서 ① immunity (면역), ② expertise (전문지식), ④ adaptation (적응)은 정답이될 수 없다."},{"q":25,"stem":"Money and the way we use it is changing. The money we use in the future might not exist in paper form at all. People are using cash less and less. People like to keep cash in their wallets for small purchases, but most people would prefer to use credit or debit cards for everything else. Cryptocurrencies such as Bitcoin may be the money of the future. In fact, Bitcoin is already in use in various places such as Scandinavia. Another alternative to cash and credit cards is the use of mobile payments. With mobile payments, a smartphone can act like a credit card. Before too long, credit cards, cash, and checks will probably be __________________.","opts":["a symbol of wealth","a thing of the past","a burden on the consumers","a means of digital exchange"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":4,"psg":null,"a":2,"ex":"지문은 현금 사용 감소 → 비트코인 같은 암호화폐의 등장 → 모바일 결제 확산이라는 흐름으로, 미래에는 기존 결제수단(신용카드·현금·수표)이 사라지거나 구식이 될 것이라고 말한다. 따라서 마지막 문장은 “얼마 안 가 신용카드, 현금, 수표는 ‘과거의 것’(구시대의 유물)이 될 것이라고 말하는 것이 가장 자연스럽다."},{"q":26,"stem":"Choose the most suitable position of the sentence below in the above passage. The key to making money is speed, not safety.","opts":["(A)","(B)","(C)","(D)"],"pts":2.0,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":0,"a":3,"ex":"박스 안에 들어 있는 문장은 ‘돈을 버는 핵심은 안전이 아니라 속도이다’라는 의미이다. (C)의 앞부분까지는 빠르게 작업을 하는 과정을 설명하고 있고 (C) 다음은 그 작업으로 인해 생기는 신체적 고통, 즉 유독가스 흡입으로 인한 위험을 강조하고 있다. 따라서 앞의 내용을 정리하면서 내용을 전환하는 네모 안의 문장은 (C)의 자리에 들어가는 것이 가장 자연스럽다."},{"q":27,"stem":"The eco-tour is not for everyone as it __________.","opts":["demands environmental activist qualifications","involves staying in a natural setting with minimal amenities","requires previous wildlife experiences","includes travel to areas with no human contact"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":1,"a":2,"ex":"지문에서 eco-tourism은 책임감 있고(responsible), 자취를 덜 남기고(low-impact travel), 불편함을 감수(roughing-it)하는 것을 포함한다고 설명한다. 5일 중 3일을 해 먹에서 자고, 햇빛, 땀, 모기, 강에서 프라이버시 없이 목욕하는 것도 감수해야 하기 때문이다. 따라서 eco-tour가 모두에게 맞지 않는 것은 ‘자연환경에서 편의시설이 최 소한으로 있는 상태에서 지내는 여행’이기 때문이다."},{"q":28,"stem":"Andrew Parker went to the Australian desert in order to ___________________________.","opts":["understand how thorny devils collect water","capture thorny devils for animal biology research","save thorny devils suffering from water scarcity in the desert","study the evolutionary adaptation of thorny devils in the desert"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":2,"a":1,"ex":"지문 마지막에 보면 Parker had come here to solve the riddle of precisely how it does this .... to make a device to help people collect water in the desert(사 람들이 사막에서 물을 모으는데 도움이 될 기구를 만들기 위해 .... thorny devil이 정 확히 물을 어떻게 끌어 모으는지, 그 수수께끼를 풀기 위해 왔다)는 내용이 나온다. 즉 Parker가 사막에 온 이유는 thorny devil이 물을 모으는 원리를 이해하기 위해서이다."},{"q":29,"stem":"Which is implied as a reason for the craftsman’s execution in the passage?","opts":["The craftsman lied, claiming his glass was unbreakable.","The craftsman made the glass far larger than what Tiberius had requested.","The new invention could destabilize the existing industrial structures.","The leakage of information could delay the onset of the Roman glass-making industry."],"pts":3.0,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":3,"a":3,"ex":"지문의 마지막 부분을 보면 such an invention would have disrupted Rome’s important glass industry(그런 발명은 로마의 중요한 유리 산업을 붕괴시켰을 것이다)라고 나와 있다. 이를 통해 장인이 만든 깨지지 않는다는 유리가 도입되면 기존 유리 산업에 큰 타격이 되므로 황제가 그것을 막기 위해 그 장인을 처형했을 가능성이 암시되고 있음을 알 수 있다."},{"q":30,"stem":"Which is the most suitable for the blank?","opts":["are considered normal food","are consumed in combination","are produced in North America","are regarded as a balanced diet"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":4,"a":1,"ex":"meat and potatoes kind of person은 특별한 음식보다 평범하고 기본적인 음식을 좋아하는 사람이라는 뜻이다. 따라서 이 표현은 문화적으로 고기와 감자가 특별식이 아니라 기본적이고 평범한 음식으로 여겨진다는 점을 보여준다. 따라서 빈칸에는 ‘표 준적인/정상적인 음식이라고 여겨진다’가 들어가는 것이 적절하다."},{"q":31,"stem":"What is the main idea of the passage?","opts":["Cloning exerts a dominant influence on our society.","People worry about the potential risks of cloning.","Good or bad, technological progress is inevitable.","Most scientists raise ethical objections to human cloning."],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":5,"a":2,"ex":"지문의 요지는 포유류 복제가 보편화되면서 인간 복제 가능성에 대한 우려가 커지고 있다는 것이다. 과학자들은 윤리적으로 이를 받아들이기 어렵다고 보고, 기술이 악용될 위험에 대해서도 언급하지만 전체 내용은 복제 기술(특히 인간 복제)의 잠재적 위 험에 대한 사람들의 두려움과 위험을 설명한다고 보아야 한다."},{"q":32,"stem":"Which does the underlined word exploration refer to?","opts":["civilization","migration","colonization","integration"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":6,"a":3,"ex":"지문에서 exploration은 단순히 ‘탐험’이 아니라, 섬들을 찾아가고 그곳에 정착하여 식민지를 만들고 영역을 확장하는 활동을 의미한다. 즉 새로운 ‘탐험의 시기’는 새로 운 섬으로 나아가 정착지를 세우는 과정, 곧 colonization(식민/정착)이다."},{"q":33,"stem":"Which is the most important for survival?","opts":["Handling the right tools","Being able to trap animals to eat","Getting enough physical training","Having distinctive personal qualities"],"pts":2.0,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":7,"a":4,"ex":"지문에는 장비 없어도 살아남은 경우가 있었고, 도구가 충분해도 살아남지 못한 경 우가 있다고 나온다. 그래서 생존에 더 중요한 것은 역경(adversity)을 어떻게 견디고 대처하느냐라고 말하므로 개인의 성격/인격이 생존에 가장 핵심적인 요소라고 말한다. 따라서 생존에 가장 중요한 요소는 ④개인의 독특한 자질(셩격/대처 능력)이다."},{"q":34,"stem":"Which is the most suitable for the blank?","opts":["confident","forthcoming","apprehensive","persevering"],"pts":3.0,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":8,"a":2,"ex":"빈칸이 들어가 있는 문장은 ‘아이디어를 도난당할까 봐 제품에 대해 다 털어놓고 밝 히지 않는다’는 의미가 되어야 한다. 따라서 빈칸에는 ‘정보를 기꺼이 제공하는, 숨김 없이 말하는’이라는 의미의 forthcoming이 가장 자연스럽다. ① confident는 자신 있는, ③apprehensive 걱정하는, ④persevering 끈기 있는 의 의미이다."},{"q":35,"stem":"Why does Huges Vinchon mention a water soluble bag?","opts":["to convince the reader to try innovative textiles","to show a case where a product idea was stolen","to give an example of eco-friendly products by Dubar-Warneton","to evoke admiration for a fabric that can dissolve in water"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":8,"a":4,"ex":"Huges Vinchon이 자신의 회사에서 만드는 ‘놀라운’ 섬유를 보여주고 자랑하는 맥락에서 기름 흡수 섬유, 진동 흡수 섬유, 끓는 물에 넣으면 녹는 가방을 예로 들고 있다. 따라서 Vinchon이 물에 녹는 가방을 언급하는 목적은 ‘신기하고 놀라운 제품’을 보여줘서 독자가 감탄하게 하는 것이다."},{"q":36,"stem":"Which best describes Leonardo da Vinci?","opts":["He gained recognition as a master artist after his death.","He created artworks that were both enigmatic and captivating.","He was regarded as a talented technician rather than an artist.","He prioritized scientific logic over artistic soul in his masterpieces."],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":9,"a":2,"ex":"지문에서 ‘His painting are as secret and seductive as himself’라고 나와 있는데 그의 작품이 enigmatic(수수께끼 같은)하고 동시에 매혹적(captivating)이라고 설명하는 ②가 정답이다. ①은 그가 죽은 이후에 뛰어난 예술가로서 인정을 받았다는 내용 인데, 본문에 보면 그는 살아 있을 때에 이미 인정을 받았다는 내용이 나와 있고 ③ 은 그가 예술가라기보다는 재능있는 기술자로 간주되었다는 말이므로 지문의 내용과는 다르다. 다빈치는 과학적 정신과 예술적 영혼을 모두 갖추었다고 했지 과학적 논 리를 우선시했다는 내용은 없기 때문에 ④도 본문 내용과 맞지 않다."},{"q":37,"stem":"What does the underlined part mean?","opts":["Leonardo da Vinci and William Shakespeare were above average in their respective fields.","Leonardo da Vinci was a good painter as well as William Shakespeare was a smart wordsmith.","Both Leonardo da Vinci and William Shakespeare were respected as skilled professionals in their crafts.","Calling Leonardo da Vinci an excellent painter and William Shakespeare a clever wordsmith is an understatement of their talents."],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":9,"a":4,"ex":"밑줄친 부분은 레오나르도 다 빈치와 윌리엄 셰익스피어 둘 다 ‘훌륭한 화가’와 ‘문 장가’라는 말로는 그 재능을 표현하기에 부족하다는 의미이다. 즉 두 사람을 그렇게 부르는 것은 그들의 능력을 과소평가하는 말(understatement)이라고 할 수 있다."},{"q":38,"stem":"Choose the appropriate order of the paragraphs.","opts":["(A) - (C) - (B)","(B) - (C) - (A)","(C) - (A) - (B)","(C) - (B) - (A)"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":10,"a":2,"ex":"(A)는 물 부족 문제 해결의 성과를 제시한다. (B)는 Macleod가 부임했을 때의 ‘재앙 같은 상황’을 제시한다. (C)는 문제 해결을 위한 구체적 조치들을 설명한다. 따라서 문제 상황(B)→문제 해결(C)→성과(A)의 순서로 배치하는 것이 가장 자연스럽다."},{"q":39,"stem":"What is the passage mainly about?","opts":["The history of Durban’s water services","The challenges faced by Durban Metro Water Services","The successful water conservation measures in Durban","The promotion of the welfare designed by Macleod"],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":10,"a":3,"ex":"지문은 물이 낭비되고 있는 상황, 이를 해결하기 위한 절수/보수 정책, 그 정책의 결과로 나타난 물소비 감소와 댐 건설이 불필요함을 말한다. 따라서 이 글 전체의 핵 심은 Durban의 성공적인 물 절약/보존 대책이다."},{"q":40,"stem":"Which is true according to the passage?","opts":["Some of the saved budget was allocated to assist the needy.","All citizens in Durban have been ensured the free water supply.","Macleod will expand the water storage capacity due to the growth in population.","Durban addressed water shortage issues without building additional dams."],"pts":2.5,"inline":false,"sec":5,"psg":10,"a":4,"ex":"①의 절약한 예산의 일부가 가난한 사람들을 돕는데 배정되었다는 것은 본문 내용과 다르다. ②는 Durban의 모든 시민들에게는 무료 급수가 보장되었다는 내용인데 (C) 의 마지막 부분에 보면 가난한 사람들이 기본적인 급수를 받을 수 있도록 보장했다고 하므로 본문과는 일치하지 않는다. ③는 Macleod가 인구 증가 때문에 물 공급 용량을 확대할 것이라는 내용인데 (A)의 마지막 부분에 주민들이 추가로 증가해도 앞으로 수십 년 동안 새로운 댐이 필요 없을 것이라고 Macleod가 Durban시에게 확신시켰다는 말이 나오므로 본문의 내용과 맞지 않는다. ④는 추가 댐 건설 없이 물 부족 문제를 해결했다는 내용이므로 본문과 일치한다."}]}};
